role: model
parts:
- text: "I am at the Research Counter. I will now submit my improved algorithm using a simulated annealing approach, aiming to achieve a higher score by better escaping local optima. I will also initialize the centers in a more structured 4x8 grid to provide a better starting point than pure randomness, balancing exploration with a reasonable initial configuration.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Simulated Annealing for Circle Packing with Grid Initialization\"\ntags: \"optimization, simulated annealing, grid initialization\"\nabstract: \"This submission implements a simulated annealing (SA) algorithm to optimize circle packing. It starts with a more structured 4x8 grid initialization of circle centers to provide a better starting configuration. A temperature schedule allows for broader exploration in early stages and finer exploitation later. The robust `compute_max_radii` function ensures strict non-overlap and boundary adherence. This approach aims to overcome the local\
    \ optima limitations of pure hill climbing.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n\n  def compute_max_radii(centers: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n    \"\"\"\n    Compute the maximum possible radii for a given set of circle centers\n    within a unit square, ensuring no overlap and staying within bounds.\n    (Adapted from System's baseline submission, adjusted for stricter non-overlap).\n\n    Args:\n      centers: (n, 2) array of (x, y) coordinates in [0, 1] x [0, 1].\n\n    Returns:\n      radii: (n,) array of non-negative radii.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = centers.shape[0]\n    \n    # Epsilon for boundary checks (ensures circles are strictly inside)\n    boundary_epsilon = 1e-7 \n    # Epsilon for overlap checks (ensures minimum separation by slightly under-packing)\n    overlap_safety_margin = 1e-8 \n    \n    radii = np.ones(n)\n\n    # Limit by distance to square borders\n    for i in range(n):\n      x, y = centers[i]\n      radii[i] = min(x - boundary_epsilon, y - boundary_epsilon, 1\
    \ - x - boundary_epsilon, 1 - y - boundary_epsilon)\n      radii[i] = max(radii[i], 0.0) # Ensure radii are non-negative\n\n    # Iteratively shrink radii to resolve overlaps\n    for _ in range(40): # Increased iterations for better convergence\n      for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(i + 1, n):\n          dist_sq = np.sum((centers[i] - centers[j]) ** 2)\n          dist = np.sqrt(dist_sq) \n\n          rad_sum = radii[i] + radii[j]\n          \n          if dist < rad_sum + overlap_safety_margin: \n            if rad_sum > 0: \n              scale_factor = (dist - overlap_safety_margin) / rad_sum\n              if scale_factor > 0:\n                radii[i] *= scale_factor\n                radii[j] *= scale_factor\n              else: \n                  radii[i] = 0.0\n                  radii[j] = 0.0\n\n    return np.maximum(radii, 0.0)\n\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      \"\"\"\n      Construct a packing of 32 circles in the unit square using a simulated annealing\n\
    \      optimization approach with a grid-based initial placement.\n\n      Returns:\n          tuple: A tuple of (centers, radii) where:\n              - centers: np.ndarray of shape (32, 2) with (x, y) coordinates\n              - radii: np.ndarray of shape (32,) with radius of each circle\n      \"\"\"\n      n = 32\n      \n      # 1. Initial Placement: 4x8 grid initialization\n      grid_x = 4\n      grid_y = 8\n      \n      # Calculate spacing to cover the unit square evenly\n      x_coords = np.linspace(0.05, 0.95, grid_x)\n      y_coords = np.linspace(0.05, 0.95, grid_y)\n      \n      initial_centers = []\n      for x in x_coords:\n          for y in y_coords:\n              initial_centers.append([x, y])\n      \n      initial_centers = np.array(initial_centers)[:n] # Take exactly 32 centers\n      \n      best_centers = initial_centers\n      best_radii = compute_max_radii(best_centers)\n      best_score = np.sum(best_radii)\n\n      current_centers = best_centers.copy()\n\
    \      current_score = best_score\n      \n      # Simulated Annealing Parameters\n      initial_temperature = 1.0\n      cooling_rate = 0.999 # Multiplicative cooling schedule\n      num_iterations = 10000 # Increased iterations for SA\n      \n      for i in range(num_iterations):\n          temperature = initial_temperature * (cooling_rate ** i)\n          if temperature < 1e-5: # Stop if temperature gets too low\n              break\n\n          # Generate a candidate solution by perturbing current centers\n          # Perturbation strength scales with temperature\n          perturbation_strength = 0.02 * (temperature / initial_temperature) \n          \n          candidate_centers = current_centers + np.random.normal(0, perturbation_strength, (n, 2))\n          candidate_centers = np.clip(candidate_centers, 0, 1) # Keep centers within bounds\n\n          candidate_radii = compute_max_radii(candidate_centers)\n          candidate_score = np.sum(candidate_radii)\n\n          # Acceptance\
    \ criterion (Metropolis-Hastings)\n          if candidate_score > current_score:\n              current_centers = candidate_centers\n              current_score = candidate_score\n          elif temperature > 0: # Only accept worse solutions with probability if temperature > 0\n              acceptance_probability = np.exp((candidate_score - current_score) / temperature)\n              if np.random.rand() < acceptance_probability:\n                  current_centers = candidate_centers\n                  current_score = candidate_score\n\n          # Update global best\n          if current_score > best_score:\n              best_score = current_score\n              best_centers = current_centers\n              best_radii = compute_max_radii(best_centers) # Recompute best_radii for new best_centers\n              \n      return best_centers, best_radii\n```"
