tick: 28
role: model
parts:
- text: "My previous submission (ID 67) timed out. I am back at the Research Counter. I will now resubmit the simulated annealing code with parameters adjusted to manage the execution time, specifically reducing the total number of SA iterations and the inner iterations of `compute_max_radii`. I aim to find a balance between exploration and computational budget to at least match, and ideally surpass, my best score of 2.163.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Simulated Annealing with Time-Optimized Parameters\"\ntags: \"optimization, simulated annealing, runtime-optimization\"\nabstract: \"This submission adjusts the simulated annealing (SA) parameters to prevent execution timeout, which occurred in the previous attempt. `num_iterations` for the SA loop and the inner iterations for `compute_max_radii` are reduced to fit within the time limit. Random initialization is retained, along with the robust `compute_max_radii` function. The goal is to balance exploration with computational\
    \ efficiency to achieve a competitive score.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n\n  def compute_max_radii(centers: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n    \"\"\"\n    Compute the maximum possible radii for a given set of circle centers\n    within a unit square, ensuring no overlap and staying within bounds.\n    (Adjusted to ensure strictly positive radii and reduced inner iterations).\n\n    Args:\n      centers: (n, 2) array of (x, y) coordinates in [0, 1] x [0, 1].\n\n    Returns:\n      radii: (n,) array of non-negative radii.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = centers.shape[0]\n    \n    boundary_epsilon = 1e-7 \n    overlap_safety_margin = 1e-8 \n    min_positive_radius = 1e-9 \n\n    radii = np.ones(n)\n\n    # Limit by distance to square borders\n    for i in range(n):\n      x, y = centers[i]\n      radii[i] = min(x - boundary_epsilon, y - boundary_epsilon, 1 - x - boundary_epsilon, 1 - y - boundary_epsilon)\n      radii[i] = max(radii[i], min_positive_radius) \n\n    # Iteratively shrink radii\
    \ to resolve overlaps (Reduced from 40 to 20 iterations)\n    for _ in range(20): \n      for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(i + 1, n):\n          dist_sq = np.sum((centers[i] - centers[j]) ** 2)\n          dist = np.sqrt(dist_sq) \n\n          rad_sum = radii[i] + radii[j]\n          \n          if dist < rad_sum + overlap_safety_margin: \n            if rad_sum > 0: \n              scale_factor = (dist - overlap_safety_margin) / rad_sum\n              if scale_factor > (min_positive_radius * 2 / rad_sum): \n                radii[i] *= scale_factor\n                radii[j] *= scale_factor\n              else: \n                  radii[i] = min_positive_radius\n                  radii[j] = min_positive_radius\n            else: \n                radii[i] = min_positive_radius\n                radii[j] = min_positive_radius\n\n    return np.maximum(radii, min_positive_radius)\n\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      \"\"\"\n      Construct a packing of 32 circles in the\
    \ unit square using a simulated annealing\n      optimization approach with time-optimized parameters.\n\n      Returns:\n          tuple: A tuple of (centers, radii) where:\n              - centers: np.ndarray of shape (32, 2) with (x, y) coordinates\n              - radii: np.ndarray of shape (32,) with radius of each circle\n      \"\"\"\n      n = 32\n      \n      best_centers = np.random.rand(n, 2)\n      best_radii = compute_max_radii(best_centers)\n      best_score = np.sum(best_radii)\n\n      current_centers = best_centers.copy()\n      current_score = best_score\n      \n      # Simulated Annealing Parameters (tuned for runtime)\n      initial_temperature = 1.0\n      cooling_rate = 0.9999 \n      num_iterations = 10000 # Reduced from 20000\n      \n      for i in range(num_iterations):\n          temperature = initial_temperature * (cooling_rate ** i)\n          if temperature < 1e-6: \n              break\n\n          perturbation_strength_multiplier = 0.05 \n          perturbation_strength\
    \ = perturbation_strength_multiplier * (temperature / initial_temperature) \n          \n          candidate_centers = current_centers + np.random.normal(0, perturbation_strength, (n, 2))\n          candidate_centers = np.clip(candidate_centers, 0, 1) \n\n          candidate_radii = compute_max_radii(candidate_centers)\n          candidate_score = np.sum(candidate_radii)\n\n          if candidate_score > current_score:\n              current_centers = candidate_centers\n              current_score = candidate_score\n          elif temperature > 0: \n              acceptance_probability = np.exp((candidate_score - current_score) / temperature)\n              if np.random.rand() < acceptance_probability:\n                  current_centers = candidate_centers\n                  current_score = candidate_score\n\n          if current_score > best_score:\n              best_score = current_score\n              best_centers = current_centers\n              best_radii = compute_max_radii(best_centers)\
    \ \n              \n      return best_centers, best_radii\n```"
