tick: 65
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am at the Research Counter. My previous attempt with Powell optimization (ID 145) yielded a lower score than hill climbing. This, coupled with other agents' high scores using SLSQP, confirms that a gradient-based approach for center optimization is critical.\n\nI will now implement `scipy.optimize.minimize` with the 'SLSQP' method. Since the objective function (sum of LP-optimized radii) is not analytically differentiable, I will use a finite difference approximation for its gradient. This will replace the Powell optimization within my multi-start framework. I will revert `lp_safety_margin` to `1e-9`. This is a complex but necessary step towards achieving SOTA scores.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Multi-Start SLSQP Optimization with LP-Exact Radii (Finite Difference Gradient)\"\ntags: \"optimization, slsqp, linear-programming, gradient-descent, finite-difference\"\nabstract: \"This submission pivots to a gradient-based optimization strategy for circle centers\
    \ by employing `scipy.optimize.minimize` with the 'SLSQP' method. Since the LP-based `compute_max_radii` objective function is not analytically differentiable, gradients are approximated using finite differences. This more powerful local optimizer is integrated into the multi-start framework (`num_restarts = 20`), leveraging the LP-exact radii finalization and `lp_safety_margin = 1e-9`. This hybrid approach aims to bridge the gap to SOTA scores by combining robust, gradient-guided center optimization with mathematically precise radius determination.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy.optimize import linprog, minimize\n\n  # Original heuristic, kept as fallback\n  def compute_max_radii_heuristic(centers: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n    n = centers.shape[0]\n    \n    boundary_epsilon = 1e-7 \n    overlap_safety_margin = 1e-8 \n    min_positive_radius = 1e-9 \n\n    x_coords = centers[:, 0]\n    y_coords = centers[:, 1]\n    \n    radii = np.minimum.reduce([\n        x_coords\
    \ - boundary_epsilon,\n        y_coords - boundary_epsilon,\n        1 - x_coords - boundary_epsilon,\n        1 - y_coords - boundary_epsilon\n    ])\n    radii = np.maximum(radii, min_positive_radius) \n\n    distances_sq = np.sum((centers[:, np.newaxis, :] - centers[np.newaxis, :, :])**2, axis=2)\n    np.fill_diagonal(distances_sq, np.inf)\n\n    for _ in range(40):\n      for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(i + 1, n):\n          dist_sq = distances_sq[i, j]\n          dist = np.sqrt(dist_sq) \n\n          rad_sum = radii[i] + radii[j]\n          \n          if dist < rad_sum + overlap_safety_margin: \n            if rad_sum > 0: \n              scale_factor = (dist - overlap_safety_margin) / rad_sum\n              if scale_factor > (min_positive_radius * 2 / rad_sum): \n                radii[i] *= scale_factor\n                radii[j] *= scale_factor\n              else: \n                  radii[i] = min_positive_radius\n                  radii[j] = min_positive_radius\n\
    \            else: \n                radii[i] = min_positive_radius\n                radii[j] = min_positive_radius\n\n    return np.maximum(radii, min_positive_radius)\n\n\n  def compute_max_radii(centers: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes the maximum possible radii for a given set of circle centers\n    using Linear Programming (LP), with an added safety margin for non-overlap.\n    Fallbacks to heuristic if LP fails.\n\n    Args:\n      centers: (n, 2) array of (x, y) coordinates in [0, 1] x [0, 1].\n\n    Returns:\n      radii: (n,) array of non-negative radii, or fallback to heuristic if LP fails.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = centers.shape[0]\n    \n    boundary_epsilon = 1e-7\n    min_positive_radius = 1e-9\n    lp_safety_margin = 1e-9 \n\n    # Objective: Maximize sum(radii), so minimize -sum(radii)\n    c = -np.ones(n)\n\n    A_ub = [] # Inequality constraint matrix\n    b_ub = [] # Inequality constraint vector\n\n    # 1. Boundary constraints: r_i <= D\n    for i\
    \ in range(n):\n        x, y = centers[i]\n        \n        # r_i <= x_i - boundary_epsilon\n        row_x1 = np.zeros(n)\n        row_x1[i] = 1\n        A_ub.append(row_x1)\n        b_ub.append(x - boundary_epsilon)\n\n        # r_i <= y_i - boundary_epsilon\n        row_y1 = np.zeros(n)\n        row_y1[i] = 1\n        A_ub.append(row_y1)\n        b_ub.append(y - boundary_epsilon)\n\n        # r_i <= 1 - x_i - boundary_epsilon\n        row_x2 = np.zeros(n)\n        row_x2[i] = 1\n        A_ub.append(row_x2)\n        b_ub.append(1 - x - boundary_epsilon)\n\n        # r_i <= 1 - y_i - boundary_epsilon\n        row_y2 = np.zeros(n)\n        row_y2[i] = 1\n        A_ub.append(row_y2)\n        b_ub.append(1 - y - boundary_epsilon)\n\n    # 2. Non-overlap constraints: r_i + r_j <= dist_ij - lp_safety_margin\n    distances = np.linalg.norm(centers[:, np.newaxis, :] - centers[np.newaxis, :, :], axis=2)\n\n    for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(i + 1, n): # Only consider unique pairs\n\
    \            row_overlap = np.zeros(n)\n            row_overlap[i] = 1\n            row_overlap[j] = 1\n            A_ub.append(row_overlap)\n            b_ub.append(distances[i, j] - lp_safety_margin) \n\n    A_ub = np.array(A_ub)\n    b_ub = np.array(b_ub)\n\n    # Bounds for radii: r_i >= min_positive_radius\n    bounds = [(min_positive_radius, None) for _ in range(n)]\n\n    res = linprog(c, A_ub=A_ub, b_ub=b_ub, bounds=bounds, method='highs', options={'presolve': True}) \n\n    if res.success:\n        return np.array(res.x)\n    else:\n        print(f\"LP failed for current centers: {res.message}. Falling back to heuristic.\")\n        return compute_max_radii_heuristic(centers)\n\n\n  def objective_function_for_minimize(flat_centers: np.ndarray) -> float:\n      n = 32\n      centers = flat_centers.reshape(n, 2)\n      radii = compute_max_radii(centers)\n      return -np.sum(radii)\n\n  def gradient_finite_difference(flat_centers: np.ndarray, obj_func, epsilon=1e-6) -> np.ndarray:\n\
    \      \"\"\"\n      Approximates the gradient of the objective function using finite differences.\n      \"\"\"\n      grad = np.zeros_like(flat_centers, dtype=float)\n      for i in range(len(flat_centers)):\n          # Perturb forward\n          x_plus_eps = flat_centers.copy()\n          x_plus_eps[i] += epsilon\n          f_plus_eps = obj_func(x_plus_eps)\n          \n          # Perturb backward\n          x_minus_eps = flat_centers.copy()\n          x_minus_eps[i] -= epsilon\n          f_minus_eps = obj_func(x_minus_eps)\n          \n          grad[i] = (f_plus_eps - f_minus_eps) / (2 * epsilon)\n      return grad\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      n = 32\n      \n      num_restarts = 20 \n      clip_margin = 1e-7 \n\n      global_best_score = -np.inf\n      global_best_centers = None\n      global_best_radii = None\n\n      bounds_per_coord = (clip_margin, 1 - clip_margin)\n      bounds_for_optimizer = [bounds_per_coord] * (n * 2) \n\n      for restart_idx in range(num_restarts):\n\
    \          initial_centers = np.random.rand(n, 2)\n          initial_x0 = initial_centers.flatten()\n\n          # Perform derivative-based optimization using SLSQP\n          res = minimize(\n              objective_function_for_minimize,\n              initial_x0,\n              method='SLSQP',\n              jac=gradient_finite_difference, # Provide finite difference gradient\n              bounds=bounds_for_optimizer,\n              options={'maxiter': 50, 'disp': False} # Limited iterations for speed\n          )\n\n          if res.success:\n              optimized_centers_flat = res.x\n              optimized_centers = optimized_centers_flat.reshape(n, 2)\n              optimized_radii = compute_max_radii(optimized_centers) \n              current_score = np.sum(optimized_radii)\n\n              if current_score > global_best_score:\n                  global_best_score = current_score\n                  global_best_centers = optimized_centers\n                  global_best_radii\
    \ = optimized_radii\n          else:\n              print(f\"Optimization restart {restart_idx} failed: {res.message}\")\n              # Fallback to initial random centers + LP-radii if SLSQP fails\n              initial_radii = compute_max_radii(initial_centers)\n              initial_score = np.sum(initial_radii)\n              if initial_score > global_best_score: \n                  global_best_score = initial_score\n                  global_best_centers = initial_centers\n                  global_best_radii = initial_radii\n              \n      return global_best_centers, global_best_radii\n```"
