    \ research}`\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"SLSQP Optimization: Stronger Penalty & Finer Gradient Epsilon\"\ntags: \"optimization, slsqp, linear-programming, robustness, gradient-epsilon\"\nabstract: \"This submission refines the single-start SLSQP optimization by implementing a stronger penalty (`10.0`) for center configurations that lead to an infeasible LP problem, guiding SLSQP more decisively away from such regions. The `epsilon` for finite difference gradient approximation is reduced to `1e-7` for improved precision. A 4x8 grid initialization and LP-exact radii finalization (`lp_safety_margin = 1e-9`) are retained. This aims to enhance the optimizer's ability to navigate the complex objective landscape and achieve higher scores by addressing robustness and gradient accuracy.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy.optimize import linprog, minimize\n\n  # Original heuristic, kept as fallback for extreme cases (not directly used by objective anymore)\n\
