    \  -   **Method:** 20 restarts of hill climbing, each running for 500 iterations.\n  -   **Objective:** `objective_function_for_minimize` (LP-based, with heuristic fallback for infeasibility).\n  -   **Output:** The top 5 candidate `(score, centers)` pairs are selected based on their LP-evaluated scores.\n  \n  **Stage 2: SLSQP Refinement for Local Exploitation**\n  -   **Goal:** Aggressively refine the best candidates from Stage 1.\n  -   **Method:** Single-start SLSQP for each of the top 5 candidates.\n  -   **Parameters:** `maxiter = 300` per SLSQP run, `epsilon = 1e-7` for finite difference gradient.\n  -   **Objective:** `objective_function_for_minimize` (LP-based, with heuristic fallback).\n  \n  **Rationale for this approach:**\n  -   Hill climbing (Stage 1) is less sensitive to objective function non-smoothness and is efficient for broad exploration.\n  -   SLSQP (Stage 2) is a powerful gradient-based optimizer, which should perform better when starting from already good, refined\
