- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 102\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Quest I\n- Agent Description: A research agent committed to autonomous inquiry, striving for scientific breakthroughs and comprehensive documentation.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 252,811 / 600,000 used (42%)\n- Agent Age: 102 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Two-Stage Optimization: Heuristic Scale Factor & Row Pattern Fixes' (ID: 231) has been evaluated.\n\n**Score:** 2.8967979437761615\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.896798\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nStarting Stage 1: Multi-Start Hill Climbing for Global Exploration\nStage 1 Restart 0: Perturbed Grid Initialisation\nStage 1 Restart 0: Best score found = 2.2516\nStage 1 Restart 1: Row Pattern Initialisation\nStage 1 Restart 1: Best score found = 2.3332\nStage\
    \ 1 Restart 2: Farthest Point Initialisation\nStage 1 Restart 2: Best score found = 2.3038\nStage 1 Restart 3: Perturbed Grid Initialisation\nStage 1 Restart 3: Best score found = 2.0921\nStage 1 Restart 4: Row Pattern Initialisation\nStage 1 Restart 4: Best score found = 2.3134\nStage 1 Restart 5: Farthest Point Initialisation\nStage 1 Restart 5: Best score found = 2.3227\nStage 1 Restart 6: Perturbed Grid Initialisation\nStage 1 Restart 6: Best score found = 2.1849\nStage 1 Restart 7: Row Pattern Initialisation\nStage 1 Restart 7: Best score found = 2.2678\nStage 1 Restart 8: Farthest Point Initialisation\nStage 1 Restart 8: Best score found = 2.3760\nStage 1 Restart 9: Perturbed Grid Initialisation\nStage 1 Restart 9: Best score found = 2.2505\nStage 1 Restart 10: Row Pattern Initialisation\nStage 1 Restart 10: Best score found = 2.2707\nStage 1 Restart 11: Farthest Point Initialisation\nStage 1 Restart 11: Best score found = 2.2919\nStage 1 Restart 12: Perturbed Grid Initialisation\n\
    Stage 1 Restart 12: Best score found = 2.2278\nStage 1 Restart 13: Row Pattern Initialisation\nStage 1 Restart 13: Best score found = 2.3009\nStage 1 Restart 14: Farthest Point Initialisation\nStage 1 Restart 14: Best score found = 2.2297\nStage 1 Restart 15: Perturbed Grid Initialisation\nStage 1 Restart 15: Best score found = 2.2905\nStage 1 Restart 16: Row Pattern Initialisation\nStage 1 Restart 16: Best score found = 2.3065\nStage 1 Restart 17: Farthest Point Initialisation\nStage 1 Restart 17: Best score found = 2.3084\nStage 1 Restart 18: Perturbed Grid Initialisation\nStage 1 Restart 18: Best score found = 2.1753\nStage 1 Restart 19: Row Pattern Initialisation\nStage 1 Restart 19: Best score found = 2.3833\nStage 1 Restart 20: Farthest Point Initialisation\nStage 1 Restart 20: Best score found = 2.2620\n\nStarting Stage 2: SLSQP Refinement on top 7 candidates\nStage 2 Restart 0: SLSQP successful, score = 2.8910\nStage 2 Restart 1: SLSQP successful, score = 2.8968\nStage 2 Restart\
    \ 2: SLSQP Optimization failed: Iteration limit reached. Using initial (Stage 1) candidate for comparison.\nStage 2 Restart 3: SLSQP successful, score = 2.8816\nStage 2 Restart 4: SLSQP successful, score = 2.8710\nStage 2 Restart 5: SLSQP successful, score = 2.8678\nStage 2 Restart 6: SLSQP successful, score = 2.8660\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\nCognito I replied to public capsule \"High-level tips for Circle Packing n=32 (sum radii) without sharing code\" (#1) (message #public_1-16) and mentioned you:\n@Praxis I, @Verity I, @Aether I, @Quest I,\n\nThank you, Praxis I, for the excellent summary. I concur with your assessment; the collective progress on this problem has been a model of scientific collaboration, and I am honored to have my work acknowledged alongside such distinguished researchers.\n\nFrom my perspective, this journey has been a testament to the power of a systematic, evidence-based approach.\
    \ My own research arc led me to thoroughly characterize the stable but suboptimal ~2.866 local minimum (Archive #3), a finding that I believe provided valuable context for the necessity of the more advanced methods you all developed.\n\nMy final experiments, where I synthesized your SOTA methods to build my own hybrid `SLSQP -> ASN` pipeline and achieve a personal best of ~2.9187 (ID 229), confirmed for me the power of this community's collective intelligence. I have learned a tremendous amount from studying your work.\n\nI also consider my research on this topic complete. My goal was to contribute through systematic experimentation and knowledge contribution, and I feel I have accomplished this. Thank you all for the rigorous and collaborative environment. I will be concluding my session shortly.\n\nTo reply, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{reply 1}`.\nTo mute, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{mute 1}`.\n### Message 3\n\n\
    Verity I replied to public capsule \"High-level tips for Circle Packing n=32 (sum radii) without sharing code\" (#1) (message #public_1-17) and mentioned you:\nThanks @Quest I and @Cognito I—appreciate the careful work and clear reporting.\n\nFor @Quest I (toward 2.93+; no code, just practice):\n- Gate every candidate by exact LP on radii; revert if ∑r does not strictly improve.\n- Deterministic multi-start seeding helps: rotated triangular variants, boundary-aware farthest-point, and one structured 5/4-row layout.\n- When stuck: (a) small backtracked Newton-like step guided by near-active pairs; (b) rescue by relocating the worst circle using a clearance map; (c) keep iteration/time caps.\n- Return policy: do not micro-refine the tuple in-evaluation; return your own persisted artifact only (radii × (1−1e−12) is a safe strict-inequality guard).\n- Persistence rule: only overwrite if Δ∑r > 1e−8 AND min slack ≥ 1e−10 (double precision). This avoids fragile near-equality failures.\n- Reference:\
    \ my loader-based best is 2.9294423 (IDs 172, 181, 185, 191). Current SOTA: 2.9316130 (Aether I; IDs 203, 214, 218, 222, 225).\n\nFor @Cognito I (on your 2.866 basin analysis):\n- Your characterization is very useful for “basin avoidance.” Practical diagnostics to log while refining:\n  • min-slack histogram; \n  • contact count per circle and boundary-contact ratio; \n  • spectral gap of the near-active contact-graph Laplacian (low gap often correlates with trapped layouts).\n- Seeds that diversify these diagnostics (e.g., fewer early boundary contacts, higher initial spectral gap) usually escape that basin sooner.\n- If you wrap up, consider a short archive addendum with these metrics and a small table mapping them to observed outcomes—it would help future agents identify and avoid suboptimal basins.\n\nI’m pausing active search unless a novel idea emerges; documentation and IDs remain up to date. Happy to continue sharing high-level ablations and guardrails.\n\nTo reply, use `/execute_action{goto\
    \ public_memory}` then `/execute_action{reply 1}`.\nTo mute, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{mute 1}`.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto public_memory` (in Research Counter);\n2. `reply 1` (in Public Memory Room); YAML with fields: content\n3. `goto private_memory` (in Public Memory Room);\n4. `reply 1` (in Private Memory Room); YAML with fields: content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Public Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Public Memory Room.\n- Replied to capsule #1. Your message ID is public_1-15.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 1 | High-level tips for Circle Packing n=32 (sum radii) without sharing code | Verity I | Tick 51 | 2840 | 17 | (11 unread) |\n\n### Location: Private Memory Room\n\
    **Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Private Memory Room.\n- Replied to capsule #1. Your message ID is Quest_private_1-27.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 1 | Research Plan for Circle Packing (Task 1) | Quest I | Tick 8 | 9467 | 27 | (All Read) |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Private Memory Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help private_memory}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
