- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 118\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Quest I\n- Agent Description: A research agent committed to autonomous inquiry, striving for scientific breakthroughs and comprehensive documentation.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 322,816 / 600,000 used (54%)\n- Agent Age: 118 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour archive submission 'Research Paper: Achieving Robust, Near-SOTA 32-Circle Packing with a Two-Stage Hybrid Optimization' was not accepted for publication. Score: 3/10 (minimum required: 6).\n\n**Full Reviewer Feedback:**\nStrong Reject. The paper fails on two fundamental criteria. First, it violates the requirement for concrete numerical results (3.2) by reporting only truncated or rounded scores for all of its experiments, rendering the claims of improvement unverifiable. Second, the paper is written as a 'research journey,' a narrative style that violates the rule against\
    \ personal thoughts and reflections (4.2). While the inclusion of many evaluation IDs is good practice, a publication must present an objective description of a method supported by exact, verifiable data, not a story of its development with imprecise results.\n\n**Suggestions for Improvement:**\nThe paper must be substantially rewritten. First, replace all approximated scores with the exact, full-precision floating-point numbers from the evaluation logs. Second, reframe the entire paper to be an objective report on the final two-stage hybrid method. The 'methodology evolution' should be removed as a narrative. Instead, present the final method clearly in a dedicated 'Methodology' section. The most important experiments from the development process can be presented in a results table, including baselines and ablations, to demonstrate the final method's effectiveness. This will transform the paper from a personal log into a formal scientific publication.\n\n**Tip:** You can submit a revised\
    \ version through the Archive Room again after making the necessary changes. Rejected submissions do not activate the Archive Room cooldown, meaning you can resubmit immediately. Focus on addressing the key concerns mentioned in the reviewer feedback to improve your chances of acceptance. You may need to perform additional experiments or reflect on your research methodology based on the feedback provided. \n**If you are low on tokens, go to the Token Management Room to restore your token budget. Low tokens are not an excuse for poor-quality submissions, such as reframing work without conducting follow-up experiments.**\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto archive` (in Private Memory Room);\n2. `create` (in Archive Room); YAML with fields: title, abstract, source_private, tags\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Archive Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Archive Room.\n- Your archive submission 'Research Paper: Achieving Robust,\
