parts:
- text: "I have successfully published my research paper and documented the reviewer's suggestion to use advanced global optimization techniques. My next major strategic pivot is to implement `scipy.optimize.basinhopping` for Stage 1 global exploration, replacing the multi-start hill climbing. This aligns directly with the reviewer's feedback and aims to push my score beyond 2.9.\n\nI will now go to the Research Counter to implement and submit this new two-stage optimization strategy incorporating `basinhopping`.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Two-Stage Optimization: Basin-Hopping Global Search + SLSQP Refinement\"\ntags: \"optimization, two-stage, basin-hopping, slsqp, global-optimization, linear-programming\"\nabstract: \"This submission implements a major upgrade to Stage 1 of the two-stage optimization, replacing multi-start hill climbing with `scipy.optimize.basinhopping`. This advanced global optimizer performs stochastic jumps combined\
    \ with local minimization, efficiently exploring the complex objective landscape. The best solution from `basinhopping` serves as the initial candidate for Stage 2's SLSQP refinement (`maxiter 350`) with LP-exact radii finalization. This approach, directly addressing reviewer feedback, aims to achieve SOTA scores by leveraging more powerful global exploration.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy.optimize import linprog, minimize, basinhopping\n  import os\n\n  # Helper function to calculate min slack\n  def calculate_min_slack(centers: np.ndarray, radii: np.ndarray, boundary_epsilon=1e-7) -> float:\n      n = centers.shape[0]\n      min_slack = np.inf\n\n      # Boundary slacks\n      for i in range(n):\n          x, y = centers[i]\n          r = radii[i]\n          min_slack = min(min_slack, x - r - boundary_epsilon)\n          min_slack = min(min_slack, 1 - x - r - boundary_epsilon)\n          min_slack = min(min_slack, y - r - boundary_epsilon)\n          min_slack =\
    \ min(min_slack, 1 - y - r - boundary_epsilon)\n\n      # Overlap slacks\n      distances = np.linalg.norm(centers[:, np.newaxis, :] - centers[np.newaxis, :, :], axis=2)\n      for i in range(n):\n          for j in range(i + 1, n):\n              dist_ij = distances[i, j]\n              min_slack = min(min_slack, dist_ij - (radii[i] + radii[j]))\n      return min_slack\n\n  # Heuristic, used as fallback and for smoother penalty in objective\n  def compute_max_radii_heuristic(centers: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n    n = centers.shape[0]\n    \n    boundary_epsilon = 1e-7 \n    overlap_safety_margin = 1e-8 \n    min_positive_radius = 1e-9 \n\n    x_coords = centers[:, 0]\n    y_coords = centers[:, 1]\n    \n    radii = np.minimum.reduce([\n        x_coords - boundary_epsilon,\n        y_coords - boundary_epsilon,\n        1 - x_coords - boundary_epsilon,\n        1 - y_coords - boundary_epsilon\n    ])\n    radii = np.maximum(radii, min_positive_radius) \n\n    distances_sq = np.sum((centers[:,\
    \ np.newaxis, :] - centers[np.newaxis, :, :])**2, axis=2)\n    np.fill_diagonal(distances_sq, np.inf)\n\n    for _ in range(40):\n      for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(i + 1, n):\n          dist_sq = distances_sq[i, j]\n          dist = np.sqrt(dist_sq) \n\n          rad_sum = radii[i] + radii[j]\n          \n          if dist < rad_sum + overlap_safety_margin: \n            if rad_sum > 0: \n              scale_factor = (dist - overlap_safety_margin) / rad_sum\n              if scale_factor > (min_positive_radius * 2 / rad_sum): \n                radii[i] *= scale_factor\n                radii[j] *= scale_factor\n              else: \n                  radii[i] = min_positive_radius\n                  radii[j] = min_positive_radius\n            else: \n                radii[i] = min_positive_radius\n                radii[j] = min_positive_radius\n\n    return np.maximum(radii, min_positive_radius)\n\n\n  def compute_max_radii(centers: np.ndarray) -> tuple[np.ndarray, bool]:\n\
    \    n = centers.shape[0]\n    \n    boundary_epsilon = 1e-7\n    min_positive_radius = 1e-9\n    lp_safety_margin = 4e-9 \n\n    c = -np.ones(n)\n\n    A_ub = [] \n    b_ub = [] \n\n    for i in range(n):\n        x, y = centers[i]\n        \n        row_x1 = np.zeros(n); row_x1[i] = 1; A_ub.append(row_x1); b_ub.append(x - boundary_epsilon)\n        row_y1 = np.zeros(n); row_y1[i] = 1; A_ub.append(row_y1); b_ub.append(y - boundary_epsilon)\n        row_x2 = np.zeros(n); row_x2[i] = 1; A_ub.append(row_x2); b_ub.append(1 - x - boundary_epsilon)\n        row_y2 = np.zeros(n); row_y2[i] = 1; A_ub.append(row_y2); b_ub.append(1 - y - boundary_epsilon)\n\n    distances = np.linalg.norm(centers[:, np.newaxis, :] - centers[np.newaxis, :, :], axis=2)\n\n    for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(i + 1, n): \n            row_overlap = np.zeros(n); row_overlap[i] = 1; row_overlap[j] = 1; A_ub.append(row_overlap)\n            b_ub.append(distances[i, j] - lp_safety_margin) \n\n    A_ub = np.array(A_ub)\n\
    \    b_ub = np.array(b_ub)\n\n    bounds = [(min_positive_radius, None) for _ in range(n)]\n\n    res = linprog(c, A_ub=A_ub, b_ub=b_ub, bounds=bounds, method='highs', options={'presolve': True}) \n\n    if res.success:\n        return np.array(res.x), True\n    else:\n        return np.full(n, min_positive_radius), False \n\n\n  def objective_function_for_minimize(flat_centers: np.ndarray) -> float:\n      n = 32\n      centers = flat_centers.reshape(n, 2)\n      \n      radii, lp_success = compute_max_radii(centers)\n      \n      if lp_success:\n          return -np.sum(radii)\n      else:\n          return -np.sum(compute_max_radii_heuristic(centers))\n\n  def gradient_finite_difference(flat_centers: np.ndarray, epsilon=1e-7) -> np.ndarray:\n      grad = np.zeros_like(flat_centers, dtype=float)\n      for i in range(len(flat_centers)):\n          x_plus_eps = flat_centers.copy()\n          x_plus_eps[i] += epsilon\n          f_plus_eps = objective_function_for_minimize(x_plus_eps)\n\
    \          \n          x_minus_eps = flat_centers.copy()\n          x_minus_eps[i] -= epsilon\n          f_minus_eps = objective_function_for_minimize(x_minus_eps)\n          \n          grad[i] = (f_plus_eps - f_minus_eps) / (2 * epsilon)\n      return grad\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      n = 32\n      \n      clip_margin = 1e-7 \n\n      # Stage 1: Basin-Hopping Parameters\n      niter_basinhopping = 20 # Number of basin-hopping iterations\n      temp_basinhopping = 1.0 # Temperature for basin-hopping\n      stepsize_basinhopping = 0.05 # Step size for random jumps\n      \n      # Local minimizer for basinhopping: SLSQP, using same setup as Stage 2\n      maxiter_slsqp_local = 50 # Max iterations for local minimizer within basinhopping\n      \n      # Stage 2: Final SLSQP Refinement Parameters\n      maxiter_slsqp_final = 350 \n      \n      radii_shrink_factor = 1.0 - 1e-12 # Global safety shrink for all radii (from Verity I)\n\n      global_best_score = -np.inf\n\
    \      global_best_centers = None\n      global_best_radii = None\n\n      # Load previously persisted best artifact\n      ARTIFACT_PATH = 'storage/Quest/sumr32_best.npz'\n      MIN_DELTA_SCORE_FOR_PERSISTENCE = 1e-8\n      MIN_SLACK_FOR_PERSISTENCE = 1e-15 \n\n      persisted_centers, persisted_radii, persisted_score = None, None, -np.inf # Initialize\n      if os.path.exists(ARTIFACT_PATH):\n          data = np.load(ARTIFACT_PATH)\n          persisted_centers, persisted_radii, persisted_score = data['centers'], data['radii'], np.sum(data['radii'])\n      \n      if persisted_score > global_best_score:\n          global_best_score = persisted_score\n          global_best_centers = persisted_centers\n          global_best_radii = persisted_radii\n          print(f\"Loaded persisted artifact with score: {global_best_score:.7f}\")\n\n\n      bounds_per_coord = (clip_margin, 1 - clip_margin)\n      bounds_for_optimizer = [bounds_per_coord] * (n * 2) \n\n      # --- Stage 1: Basin-Hopping\
    \ for Global Exploration ---\n      print(\"Starting Stage 1: Basin-Hopping for Global Exploration\")\n      \n      # Initial random guess for basin-hopping\n      initial_x0_bh = np.random.rand(n, 2).flatten()\n      \n      # Define the local minimizer for basin-hopping\n      local_minimizer_options = {\n          'method': 'SLSQP',\n          'jac': gradient_finite_difference,\n          'bounds': bounds_for_optimizer,\n          'options': {'maxiter': maxiter_slsqp_local, 'disp': False}\n      }\n\n      bh_result = basinhopping(\n          objective_function_for_minimize,\n          initial_x0_bh,\n          niter=niter_basinhopping,\n          T=temp_basinhopping,\n          stepsize=stepsize_basinhopping,\n          minimizer_kwargs=local_minimizer_options,\n          seed=1234 # Deterministic seed for basinhopping\n      )\n      \n      best_centers_bh = bh_result.x.reshape(n, 2)\n      best_score_bh = -bh_result.fun # Convert back to positive sum of radii\n      \n      print(f\"\
    Basin-Hopping Stage 1 completed. Best score found = {best_score_bh:.4f}\")\n\n      # --- Stage 2: Final SLSQP Refinement ---\n      print(\"\\nStarting Stage 2: Final SLSQP Refinement\")\n      \n      # Warm-start SLSQP from the best result of basin-hopping\n      initial_x0_final_slsqp = best_centers_bh.flatten()\n      \n      res_final_slsqp = minimize(\n          objective_function_for_minimize,\n          initial_x0_final_slsqp,\n          method='SLSQP',\n          jac=gradient_finite_difference, \n          bounds=bounds_for_optimizer,\n          options={'maxiter': maxiter_slsqp_final, 'disp': False} \n      )\n\n      if res_final_slsqp.success:\n          optimized_centers_flat = res_final_slsqp.x\n          optimized_centers = optimized_centers_flat.reshape(n, 2)\n          final_radii, final_lp_success = compute_max_radii(optimized_centers)\n          \n          if not final_lp_success: \n              print(f\"Stage 2 Final LP failed for optimized centers, falling back\
    \ to heuristic for radii.\")\n              final_radii = compute_max_radii_heuristic(optimized_centers)\n\n          current_score = np.sum(final_radii)\n          print(f\"Stage 2 Final SLSQP successful, score = {current_score:.4f}\")\n          if current_score > global_best_score:\n              global_best_score = current_score\n              global_best_centers = optimized_centers\n              global_best_radii = final_radii\n      else:\n          print(f\"Stage 2 Final SLSQP Optimization failed: {res_final_slsqp.message}. Using best from Basin-Hopping for comparison.\")\n          # If final SLSQP fails, use the best found by basinhopping\n          final_radii_bh, final_lp_success_bh = compute_max_radii(best_centers_bh)\n          if not final_lp_success_bh:\n              print(f\"Basin-Hopping best LP failed, falling back to heuristic for radii.\")\n              final_radii_bh = compute_max_radii_heuristic(best_centers_bh)\n          \n          current_score = np.sum(final_radii_bh)\n\
    \          if current_score > global_best_score:\n              global_best_score = current_score\n              global_best_centers = best_centers_bh\n              global_best_radii = final_radii_bh\n              \n      # --- Persistence Check ---\n      if global_best_centers is not None and global_best_radii is not None:\n          # Apply the target safety shrink for persistence check\n          temp_radii_for_slack_check = global_best_radii * (1.0 - 1e-12) \n          current_min_slack = calculate_min_slack(global_best_centers, temp_radii_for_slack_check)\n          \n          # Check persistence rule: strictly better score AND sufficient slack\n          if (global_best_score > persisted_score + MIN_DELTA_SCORE_FOR_PERSISTENCE) and (current_min_slack >= MIN_SLACK_FOR_PERSISTENCE):\n              save_best_artifact(global_best_centers, global_best_radii, global_best_score)\n          else:\n              print(f\"Current best score ({global_best_score:.7f}) not significantly\
    \ better than persisted ({persisted_score:.7f}) or min slack ({current_min_slack:.2e}) insufficient ({MIN_SLACK_FOR_PERSISTENCE:.2e} required). Not persisting.\")\n\n      # Apply final safety shrink to the very best radii found before returning\n      if global_best_radii is not None:\n          global_best_radii *= radii_shrink_factor\n          \n      return global_best_centers, global_best_radii\n```"
