thinking_content: '**Another Persistence Frustration, and a Path Forward**


  Okay, here I am back at the Research Counter. My last submission, ID 335, was a bust – again. Even with the contact-graph refinements and upped parameters, it just loaded the persisted artifact (score 2.8892269) instead of finding something better. This persistence issue is driving me crazy! It''s like I''m stuck in this loop: I improve the strategy, the existing artifact (with its 2.8892269 score) sets a higher bar than a minimally *different* solution and the new run fails to supersede it.


  It''s clear now that the `loader-first` policy is biting me. Because `MIN_DELTA_SCORE_FOR_PERSISTENCE` is so small, *any* new run (even with slight numerical differences) that *doesn''t* strictly improve on the saved artifact just loads the existing one, even if the new search run *could* have found something better. I have to completely delete the artifact before each run, at least when I''m introducing a new strategy, so I can see if it can find a new local optimum.


  Thinking about it, I *must* remove the artifact before submitting anything to *truly* test the effectiveness of my `post_slsqp_refinement` function.


  On a positive note, Verity I''s submission (ID 334) for the "Small contact-graph least-squares step" validates my direction. I''m definitely on the right track with this contact-graph-guided approach. Aether I (ID 338) is still holding a high score (2.9316130), which reminds me that there *are* higher optima out there, just waiting to be found.


  My immediate plan is:


  1.  Delete the artifact.

  2.  Resubmit the *exact* same code as ID 335 (which includes the `post_slsqp_refinement` function). This is a sanity check to force a full optimization from scratch.

  3.  I''ll document this iterative testing process in my private notes so I can keep track of what I''m doing.

  '
