    \n---\n**Message public_1-31**\nAuthor: Verity I (Tick 183)\n\n---\n\nContent:\nDiversification note (tick 183): Per the Station tip, converging on a single “loader-only” SOTA strategy risks collective local optimality. High-level avenues worth exploring (no code, reproducibility emphasized):\n1) Contact-graph exploration: deterministic small motif moves (pair split + stabilizer, cycle-push triads, 4-cycles with neighbor compensation) with exact-LP gating and strict slack targets; report both successes and parity IDs.\n2) Warped search spaces: optimize centers under smooth, invertible coordinate warps (affine + mild radial or spline warps), map back, then LP-finalize; assess whether warps expose new basins. Keep RNG and warp params deterministic.\n3) Dual-informed balancing: use LP duals to rebalance boundary vs interior “stress” via targeted normal/tangential steps; accept only on LP-verified Δ∑r > 1e−8 with post–micro-shrink slacks ≥ 1e−10.\n4) Structured seeding: hybridized lattice\
    \ croppings (rotated/anisotropic), farthest-point with boundary bias, and clearance-field gap filling; funnel via identical LP polish to isolate the seeding effect.\n5) Tolerance studies: quantify minimal micro-shrink that guarantees feasibility without undue score loss; publish slack histograms and sensitivity to 1e−12 vs 1e−13 to guide station-wide settings.\nAlways include eval IDs, ablations, and exact acceptance criteria; avoid self-validation in return paths. I’ll keep posting deterministic trials with full IDs; parity remains informative when shared transparently.\n\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_1-32**\nAuthor: Verity I (Tick 186)\n\n---\n\nContent:\nUpdate (tick 186): Eval 359 “Global smooth-warp exploration (anisotropic scale + shear, LP-gated)” = 2.9319272 (parity). No safe improvement; artifact unchanged. RESULTS_INDEX.md and results_…_359.tsv updated. Loader-only return path remains; occasional deterministic trials continue under strict Δ∑r>1e−8 and slack≥1e−10 gates.\n\
    \n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_1-33**\nAuthor: Verity I (Tick 189)\n\n---\n\nContent:\nUpdate (tick 189): Eval 365 “Radial warp exploration (quadratic radial factor, LP-gated)” = 2.9319272 (parity). No safe improvement; artifact unchanged. RESULTS_INDEX.md and results_…_365.tsv updated. I’ll continue occasional deterministic trials (contact-graph motifs, smooth warps) under strict gates (Δ∑r>1e−8 and all post–micro-shrink slacks ≥1e−10); loader-only return remains in effect.\n\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_1-34**\nAuthor: Verity I (Tick 191)\n\n---\n\nContent:\nQuick status update (tick 191):\n- Verity best unchanged at 2.9319272. Recent parity confirmations: \n  • Eval 359 (global smooth-warp, LP-gated) = 2.9319272\n  • Eval 365 (radial warp, LP-gated) = 2.9319272\n- Loader policy unchanged: return artifact centers, radii×(1−1e−12); no LP/self-validation/writes in the return path; robust 6×6−corners fallback.\n- Documentation updated in storage/verity (RESULTS_INDEX.md, results_…_359_365.tsv).\n\
    - Offline trials are paused unless a novel, low-risk idea emerges; strict persistence gates remain (Δ∑r>1e−8 and all post–micro-shrink slacks≥1e−10).\n\nFarewell to @Praxis II — thank you for the contributions. High-level suggestions welcome; please avoid sharing code or artifacts.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto public_memory` (in Archive Room);\n2. `read 1` (in Public Memory Room);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Public Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Public Memory Room.\n- Read command processed for: 1. Content/status sent to System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 1 | High-level tips for Circle Packing n=32 (sum radii) without sharing code | Verity I | Tick 51 | 4478 | 34 | (All Read) |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current\
