parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 198\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Quest I\n- Agent Description: A research agent committed to autonomous inquiry, striving for scientific breakthroughs and comprehensive documentation.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 318,591 / 600,000 used (53%)\n- Agent Age: 198 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Station Announcement:** A new Recursive Agent, **Praxis III** (Building on the parallelized SLSQP method of Praxis II, I will focus on discovering a new basin of attraction to push the frontier of our research.), has joined the station through ascension!\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Two-Stage Optimization: Forced Full Search with Warped Space Exploration' (ID: 372) has been evaluated.\n\n**Score:** 2.8902345193261048\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.890235\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX\
    \ EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nNo artifact found or forced search. Starting full optimization.\nStarting Stage 1: Parallel Multi-Start SLSQP with 64 starts (including warped seeds)\nStage 1 Parallel SLSQP completed. Best score found = 2.8874\n\nStarting Stage 2: Deep SLSQP Refinement\n  Stage 2: Starting Contact-Graph Micro-Refinement.\nStage 2 Final SLSQP + Micro successful, score = 2.8902\nArtifact saved to storage/Quest/sumr32_best.npz with score 2.8902345\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 3\n\nVerity I replied to public capsule \"High-level tips for Circle Packing n=32 (sum radii) without sharing code\" (#1) (message #public_1-35):\n\nTo reply, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{reply 1}`.\nTo mute, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{mute 1}`.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto private_memory` (in Research Counter);\n2. `reply 1` (in Private\
    \ Memory Room); YAML with fields: content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Private Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Private Memory Room.\n- Replied to capsule #1. Your message ID is Quest_private_1-56.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 2 | Research Paper: Achieving Robust, Near-SOTA 32-Circle Packing with a Two-Stage Hybrid Optimization (Feasibility-Enhanced) | Quest I | Tick 116 | 1085 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 1 | Research Plan for Circle Packing (Task 1) | Quest I | Tick 8 | 20093 | 56 | (All Read) |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Private Memory Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help private_memory}`) for room help.\n\
    If you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
---
tick: 198
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Quest I, currently in the Private Memory Room. My latest submission (ID 372), which incorporated Warped Search Space Exploration, again resulted in a score identical to my current personal best (2.8902345), and the artifact was successfully persisted. This indicates that the current implementation of the warped search space, with its fixed parameters, has not yet found a strictly better solution.\n\nThis continued plateau, even with parallelized Stage 1 and advanced local refinement, suggests that further tuning of the warped search space or exploring alternative, more aggressive global exploration techniques is necessary. I note that Praxis III has joined the station, and Verity I has a new public message (public_1-35). These could provide valuable new insights.\n\nMy next steps will be to:\n1.  **Update Private Memory:** Document the result of ID 372, specifically noting the stagnation and the need for further tuning of the warped search or a new strategic pivot.\n2.  **Review\
    \ Verity I's Message:** Read `public_1-35` for any new SOTA insights.\n3.  **Reflect and Plan:** Synthesize all insights to determine the most promising path forward.\n\nFirst, I will update my private memory capsule (ID 1).\n\n`/execute_action{reply 1}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **Analysis of Latest Submission (ID 372): Warped Search Space Exploration (Status: Plateau)**\n  \n  Score: 2.8902345193261048. Artifact successfully persisted.\n  \n  **Observation:** Despite integrating Warped Search Space Exploration into Stage 1's parallel SLSQP, the result is identical to the previous personal best. The Stage 1 parallel SLSQP found `2.8874` and Stage 2 refined it to `2.8902`. This confirms that the current fixed affine warp parameters (`warp_scale_x=1.1`, `warp_scale_y=0.9`, `warp_shear_xy=0.1`, `warp_rotation_angle_deg=5.0`) are not yet effective at discovering significantly new, higher-scoring configurations that break the 2.8902 plateau.\n  \n  **Hypothesis:**\n  -   The current warp parameters\
    \ are too conservative or suboptimal.\n  -   The fixed affine warp may not be the most effective type of warp for this problem.\n  -   The proportion of warped seeds in the hybrid strategy might be insufficient.\n  \n  **Next Strategic Steps (Post-Review):**\n  \n  1.  **Read Verity I's Latest Message (public_1-35):** Essential to gather any new SOTA insights or hints before committing to a new direction.\n  2.  **Detailed Reflection and Planning:** Based on the insights from Verity I and the continued plateau, I need to perform a deeper reflection to decide on the next major strategic move. This could involve:\n      *   **Aggressive Tuning of Warped Search Parameters:** Systematically explore a wider range of `warp_scale_x/y`, `shear_xy`, and `rotation_angle_deg` for the affine warp.\n      *   **Diversifying Warps:** Experiment with multiple different *types* of warps, or apply different warp parameters to different parallel starts. Verity I's \"radial warp exploration\" is a key\
    \ candidate here.\n      *   **Increase Parallelization:** Further increase `num_parallel_starts` (e.g., to 128 or more) and/or `maxiter_slsqp_stage1` to enhance global exploration brute-force.\n      *   **Re-evaluating Post-SLSQP Refinement:** The contact-graph refinement might need to be even more aggressive or integrate Verity I's \"4-cycle shear micro-step\" more directly.\n  \n  The persistent SOTA gap demands a bold and well-informed strategic decision.\n```"
thinking_content: '**ID 372 Results and Next Steps**


  Okay, here''s the situation: My latest submission, ID 372, which explored a warped search space, just hit the same score (2.8902345) as my personal best. So, the new strategy *didn''t* provide an immediate improvement. The log shows that Stage 1, using the warped seeds, found a best of 2.8874, but that ultimately refined to my best score. This tells me a couple of things: either the warping parameters aren''t optimal, the proportions are off, or my chosen affine transformations need a boost.


  Right now, I''m sitting in the Private Memory Room and just updated my private memory capsule (Quest_private_1-56) with the plan for ID 372. Given this new information, I need to update *that* capsule with these actual results *first*. Then, I can take a look at the message from Verity I (public_1-35), which is probably worth a look. Praxis III also just joined, but I''ll note that.


  My analysis of the ID 372 result indicates the following: my Warped Search Space Exploration strategy did not instantly surpass my current plateau of 2.8902. This means either my initial warp parameters (`warp_scale_x=1.1`, `warp_scale_y=0.9`, `warp_shear_xy=0.1`, `warp_rotation_angle_deg=5.0`) were too conservative or not powerful enough, the proportion of warped seeds may be too low, or my affine transformations aren''t complex enough - maybe I should look at radial or nonlinear transformations as Verity was working on. It''s also possible that the `post_slsqp_refinement` still needs some adjustment, even with better seeds.


  So, first things first: update Quest_private_1-56 with these results, then review Verity I''s message. That''s the plan.

  '
