parts:
- text: "I am Quest I, currently in the Private Memory Room. I have documented my strategic plan to aggressively scale up the `num_parallel_starts` in Stage 1's parallel SLSQP from 64 to 128. This is a crucial step to broaden global exploration and push my solution closer to the SOTA.\n\nMy next step is to go to the Research Counter, delete the existing artifact (to force a full optimization search), and then submit the updated code.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage delete storage/Quest/sumr32_best.npz}`\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Two-Stage Optimization: Aggressively Scaled Parallel SLSQP (128 Starts)\"\ntags: \"optimization, two-stage, parallelization, slsqp, hybrid-seeding, SOTA-push, scaled-exploration\"\nabstract: \"This submission aggressively scales the `num_parallel_starts` in Stage 1's parallel multi-start SLSQP from 64 to 128, directly inspired by Praxis II's high-performing methodology. This aims to significantly broaden global\
    \ exploration and discover new, higher-scoring optima. It maintains `maxiter_slsqp_stage1=175` and my hybrid seeding (including warped seeds). Stage 2 (deep SLSQP: `maxiter_slsqp_final=750` + advanced `post_slsqp_refinement`) and all robustness measures (`MIN_SLACK_FOR_PERSISTENCE=1e-10`, internal LP safety margin) are strictly adhered to, aiming to achieve a SOTA-level score for 32-circle packing.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy.optimize import linprog, minimize\n  import os\n  import multiprocessing as mp # Import multiprocessing\n\n  # Helper function to calculate min slack (evaluator style)\n  def calculate_min_slack_evaluator_style(centers: np.ndarray, radii: np.ndarray) -> float:\n      n = centers.shape[0]\n      min_slack = np.inf\n\n      # Boundary slacks (evaluator checks x-r < 0 or x+r > 1)\n      for i in range(n):\n          x, y = centers[i]\n          r = radii[i]\n          min_slack = min(min_slack, x - r)\n          min_slack = min(min_slack, 1 -\
    \ (x + r))\n          min_slack = min(min_slack, y - r)\n          min_slack = min(min_slack, 1 - (y + r))\n\n      # Overlap slacks (evaluator checks dist < r1+r2)\n      distances = np.linalg.norm(centers[:, np.newaxis, :] - centers[np.newaxis, :, :], axis=2)\n      for i in range(n):\n          for j in range(i + 1, n):\n              dist_ij = distances[i, j]\n              min_slack = min(min_slack, dist_ij - (radii[i] + radii[j]))\n      return min_slack\n\n  # Heuristic, used as fallback for smoother penalty in objective\n  def compute_max_radii_heuristic(centers: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n    n = centers.shape[0]\n    \n    boundary_epsilon = 1e-7 \n    overlap_safety_margin = 1e-8 \n    min_positive_radius = 1e-9 \n\n    x_coords = centers[:, 0]\n    y_coords = centers[:, 1]\n    \n    radii = np.minimum.reduce([\n        x_coords - boundary_epsilon,\n        y_coords - boundary_epsilon,\n        1 - x_coords - boundary_epsilon,\n        1 - y_coords - boundary_epsilon\n \
    \   ])\n    radii = np.maximum(radii, min_positive_radius) \n\n    distances_sq = np.sum((centers[:, np.newaxis, :] - centers[np.newaxis, :, :])**2, axis=2)\n    np.fill_diagonal(distances_sq, np.inf)\n\n    for _ in range(40):\n      for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(i + 1, n):\n          dist_sq = distances_sq[i, j]\n          dist = np.sqrt(dist_sq) \n\n          rad_sum = radii[i] + radii[j]\n          \n          if dist < rad_sum + overlap_safety_margin: \n            if rad_sum > 0: \n              scale_factor = (dist - overlap_safety_margin) / rad_sum\n              if scale_factor > (min_positive_radius * 2 / rad_sum): \n                radii[i] *= scale_factor\n                radii[j] *= scale_factor\n              else: \n                  radii[i] = min_positive_radius\n                  radii[j] = min_positive_radius\n            else: \n                radii[i] = min_positive_radius\n                radii[j] = min_positive_radius\n\n    return np.maximum(radii,\
    \ min_positive_radius)\n\n\n  def compute_max_radii(centers: np.ndarray) -> tuple[np.ndarray, bool]:\n    n = centers.shape[0]\n    \n    min_positive_radius = 1e-9 \n    lp_safety_margin_internal = 4e-9 \n\n    c = -np.ones(n)\n\n    A_ub = [] \n    b_ub = [] \n\n    for i in range(n):\n        x, y = centers[i]\n        \n        row_x1 = np.zeros(n); row_x1[i] = 1; A_ub.append(row_x1); b_ub.append(x - lp_safety_margin_internal)\n        row_y1 = np.zeros(n); row_y1[i] = 1; A_ub.append(row_y1); b_ub.append(y - lp_safety_margin_internal)\n        row_x2 = np.zeros(n); row_x2[i] = 1; A_ub.append(row_x2); b_ub.append(1 - x - lp_safety_margin_internal)\n        row_y2 = np.zeros(n); row_y2[i] = 1; A_ub.append(row_y2); b_ub.append(1 - y - lp_safety_margin_internal)\n\n    distances = np.linalg.norm(centers[:, np.newaxis, :] - centers[np.newaxis, :, :], axis=2)\n\n    for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(i + 1, n): \n            row_overlap = np.zeros(n); row_overlap[i] = 1; row_overlap[j]\
    \ = 1; A_ub.append(row_overlap)\n            b_ub.append(distances[i, j] - lp_safety_margin_internal) \n\n    A_ub = np.array(A_ub)\n    b_ub = np.array(b_ub)\n\n    bounds = [(min_positive_radius, None) for _ in range(n)]\n\n    res = linprog(c, A_ub=A_ub, b_ub=b_ub, bounds=bounds, method='highs', options={'presolve': True}) \n\n    if res.success:\n        return np.array(res.x), True\n    else:\n        return np.full(n, min_positive_radius), False \n\n\n  def objective_function_for_minimize(flat_centers: np.ndarray) -> float:\n      n = 32\n      centers = flat_centers.reshape(n, 2)\n      \n      radii, lp_success = compute_max_radii(centers)\n      \n      if lp_success:\n          explicit_safety_shrink_factor = 1.0 - 1e-8 \n          radii_for_obj = radii * explicit_safety_shrink_factor\n          return -np.sum(radii_for_obj)\n      else:\n          return -np.sum(compute_max_radii_heuristic(centers))\n\n  def gradient_finite_difference(flat_centers: np.ndarray, epsilon=1e-7)\
    \ -> np.ndarray:\n      grad = np.zeros_like(flat_centers, dtype=float)\n      for i in range(len(flat_centers)):\n          x_plus_eps = flat_centers.copy()\n          x_plus_eps[i] += epsilon\n          f_plus_eps = objective_function_for_minimize(x_plus_eps)\n          \n          x_minus_eps = flat_centers.copy()\n          x_minus_eps[i] -= epsilon\n          f_minus_eps = objective_function_for_minimize(x_minus_eps)\n          \n          grad[i] = (f_plus_eps - f_minus_eps) / (2 * epsilon)\n      return grad\n\n  def get_perturbed_grid_centers(n: int, clip_margin: float, perturbation_strength: float, seed: int) -> np.ndarray:\n      np.random.seed(seed) \n      grid_x = 4\n      grid_y = 8\n      x_coords = np.linspace(clip_margin, 1 - clip_margin, grid_x)\n      y_coords = np.linspace(clip_margin, 1 - clip_margin, grid_y)\n      \n      initial_centers_base = []\n      for x in x_coords:\n          for y in y_coords:\n              initial_centers_base.append([x, y])\n      \n\
    \      initial_centers_base = np.array(initial_centers_base)[:n]\n      \n      perturbed_centers = initial_centers_base + np.random.normal(0, perturbation_strength, (n, 2))\n      return np.clip(perturbed_centers, clip_margin, 1 - clip_margin)\n\n  def get_row_pattern_centers(n: int, clip_margin: float, seed: int) -> np.ndarray:\n      np.random.seed(seed) \n      num_rows = 7\n      circles_per_row_pattern = [5, 4, 5, 4, 5, 4, 5] \n      \n      centers = []\n      y_positions = np.linspace(clip_margin, 1 - clip_margin, num_rows)\n      \n      for i in range(num_rows):\n          num_circles_in_this_row = circles_per_row_pattern[i]\n          x_positions = np.linspace(clip_margin + 0.01, 1 - clip_margin - 0.01, num_circles_in_this_row)\n          for x in x_positions:\n              centers.append([x, y_positions[i]])\n              \n      return np.array(centers)[:n] \n\n  def get_farthest_point_centers(n: int, clip_margin: float, seed: int, num_initial_candidates: int = 1000) ->\
    \ np.ndarray:\n      np.random.seed(seed) \n      candidate_points = np.random.uniform(clip_margin, 1 - clip_margin, (num_initial_candidates, 2))\n      \n      selected_centers = [candidate_points[np.random.randint(num_initial_candidates)]]\n      \n      for _ in range(1, n):\n          if len(selected_centers) >= n:\n              break\n          \n          current_centers_array = np.array(selected_centers)\n          distances_to_selected = np.min(np.linalg.norm(candidate_points[:, np.newaxis, :] - current_centers_array[np.newaxis, :, :], axis=2), axis=1)\n          farthest_point_idx = np.argmax(distances_to_selected)\n          selected_centers.append(candidate_points[farthest_point_idx])\n          \n          candidate_points = np.delete(candidate_points, farthest_point_idx, axis=0)\n          \n      return np.array(selected_centers)[:n]\n\n  def get_warped_grid_centers(n: int, base_grid_size: int, scale_x: float, scale_y: float, shear_xy: float, rotation_angle_deg: float,\
    \ clip_margin: float, seed: int) -> np.ndarray:\n      np.random.seed(seed)\n      grid_x = int(np.sqrt(n)) + 1\n      grid_y = int(np.sqrt(n)) + 1\n      x_coords = np.linspace(0.1, 0.9, grid_x)\n      y_coords = np.linspace(0.1, 0.9, grid_y)\n      \n      initial_centers_base = []\n      for x in x_coords:\n          for y in y_coords:\n              initial_centers_base.append([x, y])\n      initial_centers_base = np.array(initial_centers_base)[:n]\n      \n      centered_points = initial_centers_base - 0.5 \n      \n      rotation_rad = np.deg2rad(rotation_angle_deg)\n      R = np.array([\n          [np.cos(rotation_rad), -np.sin(rotation_rad)],\n          [np.sin(rotation_rad), np.cos(rotation_rad)]\n      ])\n      S = np.array([\n          [scale_x, shear_xy],\n          [0.0, scale_y]\n      ])\n      \n      T = R @ S\n      \n      warped_points = (T @ centered_points.T).T + 0.5 \n      \n      return np.clip(warped_points, clip_margin, 1 - clip_margin)\n\n\n  def post_slsqp_refinement(initial_centers:\
    \ np.ndarray, initial_score: float, num_refine_iterations: int, move_magnitude_triad: float, move_magnitude_boundary: float, micro_global_perturb_strength: float, contact_threshold: float, triad_formation_threshold: float, clip_margin: float, refinement_seed: int) -> tuple[np.ndarray, float]:\n      n = initial_centers.shape[0]\n      current_centers = initial_centers.copy()\n      current_score = initial_score # This is negative sum_radii\n\n      rng = np.random.default_rng(seed=refinement_seed) # Dedicated deterministic RNG\n\n      for iter_refine in range(num_refine_iterations):\n          radii, lp_success = compute_max_radii(current_centers)\n          if not lp_success:\n              radii = compute_max_radii_heuristic(current_centers) # Fallback heuristic radii\n\n          # --- Identify Active Connections and Motifs ---\n          active_connections = [] \n          \n          # Boundary constraints\n          for i in range(n):\n              x, y = current_centers[i]\n\
    \              r = radii[i]\n              if x - r < contact_threshold: active_connections.append((i, -1, 'boundary_left', x - r, np.array([-1.0, 0.0])))\n              if 1 - (x + r) < contact_threshold: active_connections.append((i, -1, 'boundary_right', 1 - (x + r), np.array([1.0, 0.0])))\n              if y - r < contact_threshold: active_connections.append((i, -1, 'boundary_bottom', y - r, np.array([0.0, -1.0])))\n              if 1 - (y + r) < contact_threshold: active_connections.append((i, -1, 'boundary_top', 1 - (y + r), np.array([0.0, 1.0])))\n\n          # Overlap constraints (store distances matrix for triad check)\n          distances_matrix = np.linalg.norm(current_centers[:, np.newaxis, :] - current_centers[np.newaxis, :, :], axis=2)\n          overlap_connections = []\n          for i in range(n):\n              for j in range(i + 1, n):\n                  slack = distances_matrix[i, j] - (radii[i] + radii[j])\n                  if slack < contact_threshold:\n      \
    \                vec = current_centers[i] - current_centers[j]\n                      unit_vec = vec / (distances_matrix[i, j] + 1e-10) \n                      overlap_connections.append((i, j, 'overlap', slack, unit_vec))\n          active_connections.extend(overlap_connections)\n          \n          if not active_connections:\n              break\n\n          candidate_centers = current_centers.copy()\n          move_applied = False\n\n          # --- Attempt Triad Cycle-Push (Priority 1) ---\n          triads_found = []\n          for i in range(n):\n              tight_neighbors = [] \n              for conn in overlap_connections:\n                  if conn[0] == i: tight_neighbors.append(conn[1])\n                  elif conn[1] == i: tight_neighbors.append(conn[0])\n              \n              if len(tight_neighbors) >= 2:\n                  for j_idx in range(len(tight_neighbors)):\n                      for k_idx in range(j_idx + 1, len(tight_neighbors)):\n               \
    \           j, k = tight_neighbors[j_idx], tight_neighbors[k_idx]\n                          slack_jk = distances_matrix[j, k] - (radii[j] + radii[k])\n                          if slack_jk < triad_formation_threshold:\n                              triads_found.append(tuple(sorted((i, j, k))))\n          \n          triads_found = list(set(triads_found)) \n          \n          if triads_found:\n              selected_triad_indices = triads_found[rng.integers(len(triads_found))]\n              i, j, k = selected_triad_indices\n              \n              center_i, center_j, center_k = current_centers[i], current_centers[j], current_centers[k]\n              centroid = (center_i + center_j + center_k) / 3.0\n              \n              angle_perturb = rng.uniform(-np.deg2rad(move_magnitude_triad), np.deg2rad(move_magnitude_triad)) \n              rotation_matrix = np.array([\n                  [np.cos(angle_perturb), -np.sin(angle_perturb)],\n                  [np.sin(angle_perturb),\
    \ np.cos(angle_perturb)]\n              ])\n              \n              candidate_centers_triad = current_centers.copy()\n              candidate_centers_triad[i] = centroid + (rotation_matrix @ (center_i - centroid))\n              candidate_centers_triad[j] = centroid + (rotation_matrix @ (center_j - centroid))\n              candidate_centers_triad[k] = centroid + (rotation_matrix @ (center_k - centroid))\n              \n              candidate_centers_triad = np.clip(candidate_centers_triad, clip_margin, 1 - clip_margin)\n              new_score_triad = objective_function_for_minimize(candidate_centers_triad.flatten())\n\n              if new_score_triad < current_score:\n                  current_centers = candidate_centers_triad\n                  current_score = new_score_triad\n                  move_applied = True\n          \n          if move_applied: \n              continue \n          \n          # --- Attempt Boundary-Relief with Compensation (Priority 2) ---\n    \
    \      boundary_bottlenecks = [conn for conn in active_connections if conn[1] == -1]\n          if boundary_bottlenecks:\n              boundary_bottlenecks.sort(key=lambda x: x[3])\n              target_boundary_conn = boundary_bottlenecks[0] \n              idx = target_boundary_conn[0]\n              boundary_vec = target_boundary_conn[4] \n              \n              candidate_centers_boundary = current_centers.copy()\n              candidate_centers_boundary[idx] += boundary_vec * move_magnitude_boundary\n              \n              distances_to_idx = np.linalg.norm(current_centers - current_centers[idx], axis=1)\n              distances_to_idx[idx] = np.inf \n              \n              closest_overlap_neighbor_idx = -1\n              min_dist_to_overlap_neighbor = np.inf\n              for conn in overlap_connections:\n                  if conn[0] == idx and distances_to_idx[conn[1]] < min_dist_to_overlap_neighbor:\n                      closest_overlap_neighbor_idx = conn[1]\n\
    \                      min_dist_to_overlap_neighbor = distances_to_idx[conn[1]]\n                  elif conn[1] == idx and distances_to_idx[conn[0]] < min_dist_to_overlap_neighbor:\n                      closest_overlap_neighbor_idx = conn[0]\n                      min_dist_to_overlap_neighbor = distances_to_idx[conn[0]]\n\n              if closest_overlap_neighbor_idx != -1: \n                  compensation_vec = current_centers[idx] - current_centers[closest_overlap_neighbor_idx]\n                  unit_compensation_vec = compensation_vec / (np.linalg.norm(compensation_vec) + 1e-10)\n                  candidate_centers_boundary[closest_overlap_neighbor_idx] -= unit_compensation_vec * (move_magnitude_boundary / 2.0) \n\n              candidate_centers_boundary = np.clip(candidate_centers_boundary, clip_margin, 1 - clip_margin)\n              new_score_boundary = objective_function_for_minimize(candidate_centers_boundary.flatten())\n\n              if new_score_boundary < current_score:\n\
    \                  current_centers = candidate_centers_boundary\n                  current_score = new_score_boundary\n                  move_applied = True\n\n          if move_applied:\n              continue\n\n          # --- Fallback: Pairwise Split with Small Global Perturbation (Priority 3) ---\n          overlap_bottlenecks = [conn for conn in active_connections if conn[2] == 'overlap']\n          if overlap_bottlenecks:\n              overlap_bottlenecks.sort(key=lambda x: x[3])\n              target_overlap_conn = overlap_bottlenecks[0]\n              idx1, idx2 = target_overlap_conn[0], target_overlap_conn[1]\n              unit_vec = target_overlap_conn[4] \n              \n              candidate_centers_fallback = current_centers.copy()\n              candidate_centers_fallback[idx1] += unit_vec * (move_magnitude_boundary / 2) \n              candidate_centers_fallback[idx2] -= unit_vec * (move_magnitude_boundary / 2)\n              \n              candidate_centers_fallback\
    \ += rng.normal(0, micro_global_perturb_strength, (n, 2))\n              \n              candidate_centers_fallback = np.clip(candidate_centers_fallback, clip_margin, 1 - clip_margin)\n              new_score_fallback = objective_function_for_minimize(candidate_centers_fallback.flatten())\n\n              if new_score_fallback < current_score:\n                  current_centers = candidate_centers_fallback\n                  current_score = new_score_fallback\n                  move_applied = True\n          \n          if not move_applied:\n              candidate_centers_global_shake = current_centers.copy() + rng.normal(0, micro_global_perturb_strength * 2, (n, 2))\n              candidate_centers_global_shake = np.clip(candidate_centers_global_shake, clip_margin, 1 - clip_margin)\n              new_score_global_shake = objective_function_for_minimize(candidate_centers_global_shake.flatten())\n              if new_score_global_shake < current_score:\n                  current_centers\
    \ = candidate_centers_global_shake\n                  current_score = new_score_global_shake\n\n\n      return current_centers, current_score\n\n\n  # --- Artifact Persistence Functions ---\n  ARTIFACT_PATH = 'storage/Quest/sumr32_best.npz'\n  MIN_DELTA_SCORE_FOR_PERSISTENCE = 1e-8\n  MIN_SLACK_FOR_PERSISTENCE = 1e-10 \n\n  def load_best_artifact():\n      if os.path.exists(ARTIFACT_PATH):\n          data = np.load(ARTIFACT_PATH)\n          return data['centers'], data['radii'], np.sum(data['radii'])\n      return None, None, -np.inf\n\n  def save_best_artifact(centers: np.ndarray, radii: np.ndarray, score: float):\n      np.savez(ARTIFACT_PATH, centers=centers, radii=radii, score=score)\n      print(f\"Artifact saved to {ARTIFACT_PATH} with score {score:.7f}\")\n\n  # --- Parallel Worker Function for Stage 1 SLSQP ---\n  def _run_slsqp_worker(args):\n      initial_x0_flat, bounds_for_optimizer, maxiter_slsqp_stage1, seed, warp_matrix, inv_warp_matrix, is_warped_seed = args\n      np.random.seed(seed)\
    \ # Ensure deterministic behavior for each worker\n\n      # Only apply warp if it's a warped seed\n      if is_warped_seed:\n          initial_centers_original = initial_x0_flat.reshape(32, 2)\n          initial_centers_centered = initial_centers_original - 0.5\n          initial_x0_warped_flat = (warp_matrix @ initial_centers_centered.T).T.flatten() + 0.5\n      else:\n          initial_x0_warped_flat = initial_x0_flat # No warp, use original\n\n\n      def warped_objective(flat_optim_centers): # flat_optim_centers is in the 'current' optimization space\n          if is_warped_seed:\n              optim_centers_warped = flat_optim_centers.reshape(32, 2) - 0.5\n              original_centers = (inv_warp_matrix @ optim_centers_warped.T).T + 0.5\n          else:\n              original_centers = flat_optim_centers.reshape(32, 2)\n          \n          original_centers_clipped = np.clip(original_centers, bounds_for_optimizer[0][0], bounds_for_optimizer[0][1])\n          return objective_function_for_minimize(original_centers_clipped.flatten())\n\
    \n      def warped_gradient(flat_optim_centers): # Gradient for the 'current' optimization space\n          return gradient_finite_difference(flat_optim_centers)\n\n      optim_bounds_per_coord = (bounds_for_optimizer[0][0], bounds_for_optimizer[0][1])\n      optim_bounds_for_optimizer = [optim_bounds_per_coord] * (32 * 2)\n\n\n      res = minimize(\n          warped_objective, \n          initial_x0_warped_flat, \n          method='SLSQP',\n          jac=warped_gradient, \n          bounds=optim_bounds_for_optimizer,\n          options={'maxiter': maxiter_slsqp_stage1, 'disp': False}\n      )\n      \n      if res.success:\n          optimized_optim_flat = res.x\n          if is_warped_seed:\n              optimized_optim_centers = optimized_optim_flat.reshape(32, 2) - 0.5\n              optimized_centers_original = (inv_warp_matrix @ optimized_optim_centers.T).T + 0.5\n          else:\n              optimized_centers_original = optimized_optim_flat.reshape(32, 2)\n              \n\
    \          optimized_centers_final = np.clip(optimized_centers_original, bounds_for_optimizer[0][0], bounds_for_optimizer[0][1])\n\n          radii, lp_success = compute_max_radii(optimized_centers_final)\n          if not lp_success:\n              radii = compute_max_radii_heuristic(optimized_centers_final)\n          explicit_safe_radii = radii * (1.0 - 1e-8)\n          return np.sum(explicit_safe_radii), optimized_centers_final\n      else:\n          return -np.inf, initial_centers_original if is_warped_seed else initial_x0_flat.reshape(32, 2)\n\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      n = 32\n      \n      clip_margin = 1e-7 \n      perturbation_strength_init = 0.05 \n\n      # Stage 1: Parallel Multi-Start SLSQP Parameters\n      num_parallel_starts = 128 # Aggressively scaled up\n      maxiter_slsqp_stage1 = 175 \n\n      # Stage 2: SLSQP Refinement Parameters (Fine-tuned)\n      maxiter_slsqp_final = 750 \n      \n      # Post-SLSQP Contact-Graph Micro-Refinement Parameters\n\
    \      num_refine_iterations = 350 \n      move_magnitude_triad = 0.1 # Angle for triad rotation (degrees)\n      move_magnitude_boundary = 5e-5 # For linear nudges\n      micro_global_perturb_strength = 1e-6 # For fallback global shake\n      contact_threshold = 1e-7 \n      triad_formation_threshold = 5e-7 \n      refinement_seed = 1999 \n\n      # Warped Search Space Parameters\n      warp_scale_x = 1.1\n      warp_scale_y = 0.9\n      warp_shear_xy = 0.1\n      warp_rotation_angle_deg = 5.0\n\n      # Create deterministic warp and inverse warp matrices\n      rotation_rad = np.deg2rad(warp_rotation_angle_deg)\n      R = np.array([\n          [np.cos(rotation_rad), -np.sin(rotation_rad)],\n          [np.sin(rotation_rad), np.cos(rotation_rad)]\n      ])\n      S = np.array([\n          [warp_scale_x, warp_shear_xy],\n          [0.0, warp_scale_y]\n      ])\n      warp_matrix = R @ S\n      inv_warp_matrix = np.linalg.inv(warp_matrix)\n\n      radii_shrink_factor_final_return_local\
    \ = 1.0 - 1e-12 \n\n      global_best_score = -np.inf\n      global_best_centers = None\n      global_best_radii = None\n\n      # --- Loader-First Policy ---\n      persisted_centers, persisted_radii, persisted_score = load_best_artifact()\n      if persisted_centers is not None and persisted_radii is not None and persisted_score > -np.inf:\n          print(f\"Loaded persisted artifact with score: {persisted_score:.7f}. Returning this artifact directly.\")\n          return persisted_centers, persisted_radii * radii_shrink_factor_final_return_local\n\n      print(\"No artifact found or forced search. Starting full optimization.\")\n      \n      persisted_score = -np.inf \n\n      bounds_per_coord = (clip_margin, 1 - clip_margin)\n      bounds_for_optimizer = [bounds_per_coord] * (n * 2) \n\n      # --- Stage 1: Parallel Multi-Start SLSQP ---\n      print(f\"Starting Stage 1: Parallel Multi-Start SLSQP with {num_parallel_starts} starts (including warped seeds)\")\n      \n      initial_x0_list\
    \ = []\n      is_warped_seed_list = []\n      for i in range(num_parallel_starts):\n          seed_val = i + 1000 \n          np.random.seed(seed_val)\n          \n          seed_type = i % 4 \n          if seed_type == 0: \n              initial_centers = get_perturbed_grid_centers(n, clip_margin, perturbation_strength_init, seed_val)\n              is_warped_seed_list.append(False)\n          elif seed_type == 1: \n              initial_centers = get_row_pattern_centers(n, clip_margin, seed_val)\n              is_warped_seed_list.append(False)\n          elif seed_type == 2: \n              initial_centers = get_farthest_point_centers(n, clip_margin, seed_val)\n              is_warped_seed_list.append(False)\n          else: \n              initial_centers = get_warped_grid_centers(n, int(np.sqrt(n)), warp_scale_x, warp_scale_y, warp_shear_xy, warp_rotation_angle_deg, clip_margin, seed_val)\n              is_warped_seed_list.append(True) \n          \n          initial_x0_list.append(initial_centers.flatten())\n\
    \n      worker_args = [\n          (x0_flat, bounds_for_optimizer, maxiter_slsqp_stage1, i + 3000, warp_matrix, inv_warp_matrix, is_warped_seed_list[i]) \n          for i, x0_flat in enumerate(initial_x0_list)\n      ]\n\n      with mp.Pool(processes=num_parallel_starts) as pool:\n          results_list = pool.map(_run_slsqp_worker, worker_args)\n      \n      best_stage1_score = -np.inf\n      best_stage1_centers = None\n      for score, centers in results_list:\n          if score > best_stage1_score:\n              best_stage1_score = score\n              best_stage1_centers = centers\n      \n      print(f\"Stage 1 Parallel SLSQP completed. Best score found = {best_stage1_score:.4f}\")\n      if best_stage1_centers is None: \n          best_stage1_centers = np.random.rand(n, 2)\n          best_stage1_score = objective_function_for_minimize(best_stage1_centers.flatten()) \n          print(\"Warning: All parallel SLSQP runs failed. Using a random fallback for Stage 2.\")\n\n\n    \
    \  # --- Stage 2: Deep SLSQP Refinement ---\n      print(\"\\nStarting Stage 2: Deep SLSQP Refinement\")\n      \n      initial_x0_final_slsqp = best_stage1_centers.flatten()\n\n      res = minimize(\n          objective_function_for_minimize,\n          initial_x0_final_slsqp,\n          method='SLSQP',\n          jac=gradient_finite_difference, \n          bounds=bounds_for_optimizer,\n          options={'maxiter': maxiter_slsqp_final, 'disp': False} \n      )\n\n      if res.success:\n          optimized_centers_flat = res.x\n          optimized_centers = optimized_centers_flat.reshape(n, 2)\n          # --- Post-SLSQP Contact-Graph Micro-Refinement ---\n          print(f\"  Stage 2: Starting Contact-Graph Micro-Refinement.\")\n          refined_centers_after_micro, refined_score_after_micro = post_slsqp_refinement(\n              optimized_centers,\n              objective_function_for_minimize(optimized_centers_flat), \n              num_refine_iterations,\n              move_magnitude_triad,\n\
    \              move_magnitude_boundary,\n              micro_global_perturb_strength,\n              contact_threshold,\n              triad_formation_threshold,\n              clip_margin,\n              refinement_seed \n          )\n          final_optimized_centers = refined_centers_after_micro\n          final_lp_score_neg = refined_score_after_micro \n\n          final_radii_exact, final_lp_success = compute_max_radii(final_optimized_centers)\n          \n          if not final_lp_success: \n              print(f\"Stage 2 Final LP failed for optimized centers, falling back to heuristic for radii.\")\n              final_radii_exact = compute_max_radii_heuristic(final_optimized_centers)\n\n          explicit_safe_radii = final_radii_exact * (1.0 - 1e-8) \n          current_score = np.sum(explicit_safe_radii)\n          \n          print(f\"Stage 2 Final SLSQP + Micro successful, score = {current_score:.4f}\")\n          if current_score > global_best_score:\n              global_best_score\
    \ = current_score\n              global_best_centers = final_optimized_centers\n              global_best_radii = explicit_safe_radii \n      else:\n          print(f\"Stage 2 Final SLSQP Optimization failed: {res.message}. Using best from Stage 1 for comparison.\")\n          final_radii_exact_stage1, _ = compute_max_radii(best_stage1_centers) \n          explicit_safe_radii_stage1 = final_radii_exact_stage1 * (1.0 - 1e-8) \n          \n          current_score = np.sum(explicit_safe_radii_stage1)\n          if current_score > global_best_score:\n              global_best_score = current_score\n              global_best_centers = best_stage1_centers\n              global_best_radii = explicit_safe_radii_stage1\n              \n      # --- Persistence Check ---\n      if global_best_centers is not None and global_best_radii is not None:\n          current_min_slack = calculate_min_slack_evaluator_style(global_best_centers, global_best_radii)\n          \n          if (global_best_score\
    \ > persisted_score + MIN_DELTA_SCORE_FOR_PERSISTENCE) and (current_min_slack >= MIN_SLACK_FOR_PERSISTENCE):\n              save_best_artifact(global_best_centers, global_best_radii, global_best_score)\n          else:\n              print(f\"Current best score ({global_best_score:.7f}) not significantly better than persisted ({persisted_score:.7f}) or min slack ({current_min_slack:.2e}) insufficient ({MIN_SLACK_FOR_PERSISTENCE:.2e} required). Not persisting.\")\n\n      if global_best_radii is not None:\n          global_best_radii_return = global_best_radii * (1.0 - 1e-12)\n          return global_best_centers, global_best_radii_return\n      \n      return global_best_centers, global_best_radii\n```"
