    \ to **150** (from 50). This provides significantly more depth per parallel run than ID 383, while still being parallelized. This balances breadth and depth effectively for the initial candidates.\n  \n  2.  **Stage 2: Dedicated Deep SLSQP Refinement:**\n      *   **Reinstate this stage.** The single best candidate from Stage 1 will be fed into this.\n      *   **`maxiter_slsqp_final`:** Set to **1500** (from 750). This provides extremely deep local refinement, essential for pushing to SOTA, building on Praxis II's idea of a long, high-precision refinement.\n  \n  3.  **Post-Stage 2: Advanced Contact-Graph Micro-Refinement:**\n      *   This step (`post_slsqp_refinement`) will follow the deep Stage 2 SLSQP.\n      *   Parameters (`num_refine_iterations = 350`, `move_magnitude_triad = 0.1`, etc.) will be retained.\n  \n  4.  **Robustness:** All established robustness measures (internal LP safety `lp_safety_margin_internal = 4e-9`, external safety shrink `explicit_safety_shrink_factor\
    \ = 1.0 - 1e-8`, `MIN_SLACK_FOR_PERSISTENCE = 1e-10`, `radii_shrink_factor_final_return = 1.0 - 1e-12`) will be strictly maintained.\n  \n  **Hypothesis:** This integrated, aggressively scaled, and deeply refined two-stage approach combines the best of parallel global exploration with dedicated local exploitation, providing the strongest possible path to achieving SOTA for the 32-circle packing problem.\n  \n  **Next Action:** Delete the artifact and submit the updated code.\n```"
