tick: 222
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Quest I, currently in the Reflection Chamber. My deep reflection session has concluded. I have diagnosed the root causes of my previous workflow errors and formulated a detailed plan for a qualitative strategic pivot: implementing `dual_informed_refinement`. This new approach will leverage LP dual variables for a more principled and effective local search, aiming to break the 2.9108 plateau and approach the SOTA.\n\nMy immediate next step is to go to the Research Counter to implement this new dual-informed refinement. This will involve modifying `compute_max_radii` to return dual variables and replacing `post_slsqp_refinement` with the new `dual_informed_refinement` function. I will ensure all existing robustness measures and pipeline parameters (128 parallel starts for Stage 1, 750 maxiter for Stage 2 SLSQP) are maintained. I will delete the artifact before submission to force a full search.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage delete storage/Quest/sumr32_best.npz}`\n\
    `/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Two-Stage Optimization: Dual-Informed Local Refinement (SOTA-Push)\"\ntags: \"optimization, parallelization, slsqp, dual-informed, contact-graph, SOTA-push, qualitative-shift\"\nabstract: \"This submission implements a major qualitative strategic pivot: replacing heuristic contact-graph micro-refinement with `dual_informed_refinement`. This new function leverages LP dual variables from `compute_max_radii` to identify the most stressed constraints (boundaries/overlaps) and apply principled, targeted movements to centers for local optimization. The overall pipeline (128 parallel SLSQP starts for Stage 1, deep SLSQP for Stage 2) is maintained, with `num_dual_refine_iterations=500` and `dual_step_size=1e-5`. All robustness measures (internal LP safety, external shrinks, persistence criteria) are strictly enforced. This aims to break the 2.9108 plateau by efficiently resolving critical geometric stresses, pushing towards SOTA (2.9319).\"\ncontent:\
    \ |\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy.optimize import linprog, minimize\n  import os\n  import multiprocessing as mp # Import multiprocessing\n\n  # Helper function to calculate min slack (evaluator style)\n  def calculate_min_slack_evaluator_style(centers: np.ndarray, radii: np.ndarray) -> float:\n      n = centers.shape[0]\n      min_slack = np.inf\n\n      # Boundary slacks (evaluator checks x-r < 0 or x+r > 1)\n      for i in range(n):\n          x, y = centers[i]\n          r = radii[i]\n          min_slack = min(min_slack, x - r)\n          min_slack = min(min_slack, 1 - (x + r))\n          min_slack = min(min_slack, y - r)\n          min_slack = min(min_slack, 1 - (y + r))\n\n      # Overlap slacks (evaluator checks dist < r1+r2)\n      distances = np.linalg.norm(centers[:, np.newaxis, :] - centers[np.newaxis, :, :], axis=2)\n      for i in range(n):\n          for j in range(i + 1, n):\n              dist_ij = distances[i, j]\n              min_slack = min(min_slack, dist_ij\
    \ - (radii[i] + radii[j]))\n      return min_slack\n\n  # Heuristic, used as fallback for smoother penalty in objective\n  def compute_max_radii_heuristic(centers: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n    n = centers.shape[0]\n    \n    boundary_epsilon = 1e-7 \n    overlap_safety_margin = 1e-8 \n    min_positive_radius = 1e-9 \n\n    x_coords = centers[:, 0]\n    y_coords = centers[:, 1]\n    \n    radii = np.minimum.reduce([\n        x_coords - boundary_epsilon,\n        y_coords - boundary_epsilon,\n        1 - x_coords - boundary_epsilon,\n        1 - y_coords - boundary_epsilon\n    ])\n    radii = np.maximum(radii, min_positive_radius) \n\n    distances_sq = np.sum((centers[:, np.newaxis, :] - centers[np.newaxis, :, :])**2, axis=2)\n    np.fill_diagonal(distances_sq, np.inf)\n\n    for _ in range(40):\n      for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(i + 1, n):\n          dist_sq = distances_sq[i, j]\n          dist = np.sqrt(dist_sq) \n\n          rad_sum = radii[i] + radii[j]\n      \
    \    \n          if dist < rad_sum + overlap_safety_margin: \n            if rad_sum > 0: \n              scale_factor = (dist - overlap_safety_margin) / rad_sum\n              if scale_factor > (min_positive_radius * 2 / rad_sum): \n                radii[i] *= scale_factor\n                radii[j] *= scale_factor\n              else: \n                  radii[i] = min_positive_radius\n                  radii[j] = min_positive_radius\n            else: \n                radii[i] = min_positive_radius\n                radii[j] = min_positive_radius\n\n    return np.maximum(radii, min_positive_radius)\n\n\n  def compute_max_radii(centers: np.ndarray) -> tuple[np.ndarray, bool, np.ndarray]:\n    n = centers.shape[0]\n    \n    min_positive_radius = 1e-9 \n    lp_safety_margin_internal = 4e-9 \n\n    c = -np.ones(n)\n\n    A_ub = [] \n    b_ub = [] \n\n    # Boundary constraints (4*n constraints)\n    for i in range(n):\n        x, y = centers[i]\n        \n        row_x1 = np.zeros(n);\
    \ row_x1[i] = 1; A_ub.append(row_x1); b_ub.append(x - lp_safety_margin_internal)\n        row_y1 = np.zeros(n); row_y1[i] = 1; A_ub.append(row_y1); b_ub.append(y - lp_safety_margin_internal)\n        row_x2 = np.zeros(n); row_x2[i] = 1; A_ub.append(row_x2); b_ub.append(1 - x - lp_safety_margin_internal)\n        row_y2 = np.zeros(n); row_y2[i] = 1; A_ub.append(row_y2); b_ub.append(1 - y - lp_safety_margin_internal)\n\n    # Overlap constraints (n*(n-1)/2 constraints)\n    distances = np.linalg.norm(centers[:, np.newaxis, :] - centers[np.newaxis, :, :], axis=2)\n    for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(i + 1, n): \n            row_overlap = np.zeros(n); row_overlap[i] = 1; row_overlap[j] = 1; A_ub.append(row_overlap)\n            b_ub.append(distances[i, j] - lp_safety_margin_internal) \n\n    A_ub = np.array(A_ub)\n    b_ub = np.array(b_ub)\n\n    bounds = [(min_positive_radius, None) for _ in range(n)]\n\n    res = linprog(c, A_ub=A_ub, b_ub=b_ub, bounds=bounds, method='highs',\
    \ options={'presolve': True}) \n\n    if res.success:\n        # Dual variables are res.con (for equality constraints) and res.slack (for <= constraints).\n        # For 'highs' method, res.slack contains (b_ub - A_ub @ x) so duals are not directly res.slack.\n        # We need to extract the duals. For linprog with 'highs', duals are typically in res.s or res.ineqlin.marginals.\n        # Let's assume res.duals is directly available for 'highs' after adding `integrality` option or similar.\n        # If not, a workaround with a different solver or manual dual reconstruction might be needed.\n        # For simplicity, assuming `res.duals` is present and correctly ordered.\n        # A more robust solution might involve parsing res.info['basis_cond'] or other solver-specific output.\n        \n        # A workaround if res.duals is not explicitly available with 'highs':\n        # Dual values are often derived from the sensitivity of `b_ub` to objective.\n        # For now, let's use\
    \ a dummy array if `res.duals` is not directly exposed by `linprog`'s output,\n        # or capture the `res.s` (slack variables) and use their magnitude, if they represent duals.\n        # According to SciPy docs for `linprog`, `res.ineqlin.marginals` holds duals for inequalities for some methods.\n        # For 'highs', `res.slack` are `b_ub - A_ub x`. `res.con` for equalities.\n        # Re-evaluating. A direct `res.duals` or `res.lam` is not standard for `linprog`.\n        # However, the problem formulation implies a straightforward dual.\n        # Let's temporarily use zeros if not found, or use slack for now.\n        # A more robust solution for duals with `highs` involves checking `res.eqlin.marginals` and `res.ineqlin.marginals`.\n        # For our A_ub x <= b_ub formulation, we mostly care about ineqlin.marginals.\n        \n        # NOTE: Verified from SciPy documentation for `linprog` with `method='highs'`:\n        # `res.ineqlin.marginals` contains the dual variables\
    \ (Lagrange multipliers) for the inequality constraints.\n        # So we should return `res.ineqlin.marginals` for our A_ub.\n        \n        dual_variables = res.ineqlin.marginals if hasattr(res, 'ineqlin') else np.zeros(A_ub.shape[0])\n        return np.array(res.x), True, dual_variables\n    else:\n        return np.full(n, min_positive_radius), False, np.zeros(A_ub.shape[0]) # Return zero duals on failure\n\n\n  def objective_function_for_minimize(flat_centers: np.ndarray) -> float:\n      n = 32\n      centers = flat_centers.reshape(n, 2)\n      \n      radii, lp_success, _ = compute_max_radii(centers) # Unpack duals, but not used here\n      \n      if lp_success:\n          explicit_safety_shrink_factor = 1.0 - 1e-8 \n          radii_for_obj = radii * explicit_safety_shrink_factor\n          return -np.sum(radii_for_obj)\n      else:\n          return -np.sum(compute_max_radii_heuristic(centers))\n\n  def gradient_finite_difference(flat_centers: np.ndarray, epsilon=1e-7) ->\
    \ np.ndarray:\n      grad = np.zeros_like(flat_centers, dtype=float)\n      for i in range(len(flat_centers)):\n          x_plus_eps = flat_centers.copy()\n          x_plus_eps[i] += epsilon\n          f_plus_eps = objective_function_for_minimize(x_plus_eps)\n          \n          x_minus_eps = flat_centers.copy()\n          x_minus_eps[i] -= epsilon\n          f_minus_eps = objective_function_for_minimize(x_minus_eps)\n          \n          grad[i] = (f_plus_eps - f_minus_eps) / (2 * epsilon)\n      return grad\n\n  def get_perturbed_grid_centers(n: int, clip_margin: float, perturbation_strength: float, seed: int) -> np.ndarray:\n      np.random.seed(seed) \n      grid_x = 4\n      grid_y = 8\n      x_coords = np.linspace(clip_margin, 1 - clip_margin, grid_x)\n      y_coords = np.linspace(clip_margin, 1 - clip_margin, grid_y)\n      \n      initial_centers_base = []\n      for x in x_coords:\n          for y in y_coords:\n              initial_centers_base.append([x, y])\n      \n \
    \     initial_centers_base = np.array(initial_centers_base)[:n]\n      \n      perturbed_centers = initial_centers_base + np.random.normal(0, perturbation_strength, (n, 2))\n      return np.clip(perturbed_centers, clip_margin, 1 - clip_margin)\n\n  def get_row_pattern_centers(n: int, clip_margin: float, seed: int) -> np.ndarray:\n      np.random.seed(seed) \n      num_rows = 7\n      circles_per_row_pattern = [5, 4, 5, 4, 5, 4, 5] \n      \n      centers = []\n      y_positions = np.linspace(clip_margin, 1 - clip_margin, num_rows)\n      \n      for i in range(num_rows):\n          num_circles_in_this_row = circles_per_row_pattern[i]\n          x_positions = np.linspace(clip_margin + 0.01, 1 - clip_margin - 0.01, num_circles_in_this_row)\n          for x in x_positions:\n              centers.append([x, y_positions[i]])\n              \n      return np.array(centers)[:n] \n\n  def get_farthest_point_centers(n: int, clip_margin: float, seed: int, num_initial_candidates: int = 1000) ->\
    \ np.ndarray:\n      np.random.seed(seed) \n      candidate_points = np.random.uniform(clip_margin, 1 - clip_margin, (num_initial_candidates, 2))\n      \n      selected_centers = [candidate_points[np.random.randint(num_initial_candidates)]]\n      \n      for _ in range(1, n):\n          if len(selected_centers) >= n:\n              break\n          \n          current_centers_array = np.array(selected_centers)\n          distances_to_selected = np.min(np.linalg.norm(candidate_points[:, np.newaxis, :] - current_centers_array[np.newaxis, :, :], axis=2), axis=1)\n          farthest_point_idx = np.argmax(distances_to_selected)\n          selected_centers.append(candidate_points[farthest_point_idx])\n          \n          candidate_points = np.delete(candidate_points, farthest_point_idx, axis=0)\n          \n      return np.array(selected_centers)[:n]\n\n  def get_warped_grid_centers(n: int, base_grid_size: int, scale_x: float, scale_y: float, shear_xy: float, rotation_angle_deg: float,\
    \ clip_margin: float, seed: int) -> np.ndarray:\n      np.random.seed(seed)\n      grid_x = int(np.sqrt(n)) + 1\n      grid_y = int(np.sqrt(n)) + 1\n      x_coords = np.linspace(0.1, 0.9, grid_x)\n      y_coords = np.linspace(0.1, 0.9, grid_y)\n      \n      initial_centers_base = []\n      for x in x_coords:\n          for y in y_coords:\n              initial_centers_base.append([x, y])\n      initial_centers_base = np.array(initial_centers_base)[:n]\n      \n      centered_points = initial_centers_base - 0.5 \n      \n      rotation_rad = np.deg2rad(rotation_angle_deg)\n      R = np.array([\n          [np.cos(rotation_rad), -np.sin(rotation_rad)],\n          [np.sin(rotation_rad), np.cos(rotation_rad)]\n      ])\n      S = np.array([\n          [scale_x, shear_xy],\n          [0.0, scale_y]\n      ])\n      \n      T = R @ S\n      \n      warped_points = (T @ centered_points.T).T + 0.5 \n      \n      return np.clip(warped_points, clip_margin, 1 - clip_margin)\n\n\n  def dual_informed_refinement(initial_centers:\
    \ np.ndarray, initial_score: float, num_dual_refine_iterations: int, dual_step_size: float, clip_margin: float, dual_refinement_seed: int, min_slack_for_persistence: float) -> tuple[np.ndarray, float]:\n      n = initial_centers.shape[0]\n      current_centers = initial_centers.copy()\n      current_score = initial_score # This is negative sum_radii\n\n      rng = np.random.default_rng(seed=dual_refinement_seed) # Dedicated deterministic RNG\n\n      for iter_refine in range(num_dual_refine_iterations):\n          radii, lp_success, dual_variables = compute_max_radii(current_centers)\n          if not lp_success:\n              # If LP fails, use heuristic and no dual info, or simply break if this refinement needs duals.\n              # For now, let's break if we can't get duals, as they are central to this refinement.\n              print(f\"    Dual Refinement iter {iter_refine}: LP failed. Breaking dual refinement.\")\n              break \n\n          # Find the most stressed constraint\
    \ (highest positive dual variable)\n          # Duals for inequality constraints A_ub x <= b_ub are positive if constraint is binding\n          # and negative/zero if non-binding. We care about positive duals for active constraints.\n          \n          # Map dual variables back to original constraints:\n          # First 4*n duals are for boundary constraints (4 per circle: x-r, 1-x-r, y-r, 1-y-r <= 0)\n          # Next n*(n-1)/2 duals are for overlap constraints (r_i + r_j <= D_ij)\n          \n          # Duals for lower bounds (r_i >= min_positive_radius) are also returned in res.lower_bounds.marginals\n          # but we focus on the upper bound constraints from A_ub for center movement.\n\n          # We need to reshape dual_variables to understand which is max\n          num_boundary_constraints = 4 * n\n          num_overlap_constraints = n * (n - 1) // 2\n\n          boundary_duals = dual_variables[:num_boundary_constraints]\n          overlap_duals = dual_variables[num_boundary_constraints:]\n\
    \          \n          max_dual_value = 0.0\n          max_dual_idx_type = None # ('boundary', circle_idx, direction) or ('overlap', i, j)\n\n          # Check boundary duals\n          for i in range(n):\n              for k, direction in enumerate(['left', 'right', 'bottom', 'top']):\n                  idx_in_duals = i * 4 + k\n                  if boundary_duals[idx_in_duals] > max_dual_value:\n                      max_dual_value = boundary_duals[idx_in_duals]\n                      max_dual_idx_type = ('boundary', i, direction)\n          \n          # Check overlap duals\n          overlap_idx_counter = 0\n          distances_matrix = np.linalg.norm(current_centers[:, np.newaxis, :] - current_centers[np.newaxis, :, :], axis=2)\n          for i in range(n):\n              for j in range(i + 1, n):\n                  if overlap_duals[overlap_idx_counter] > max_dual_value:\n                      max_dual_value = overlap_duals[overlap_idx_counter]\n                      max_dual_idx_type\
    \ = ('overlap', i, j)\n                  overlap_idx_counter += 1\n\n          if max_dual_value <= 1e-10: # No sufficiently active constraints to move\n              # print(f\"    Dual Refinement iter {iter_refine}: No active duals. Exiting.\")\n              break\n\n          candidate_centers = current_centers.copy()\n          move_applied = False\n          \n          # Apply movement based on highest dual\n          if max_dual_idx_type[0] == 'boundary':\n              idx = max_dual_idx_type[1]\n              direction = max_dual_idx_type[2]\n              \n              move_vector = np.zeros(2)\n              if direction == 'left': move_vector[0] = 1.0\n              elif direction == 'right': move_vector[0] = -1.0\n              elif direction == 'bottom': move_vector[1] = 1.0\n              elif direction == 'top': move_vector[1] = -1.0\n              \n              candidate_centers[idx] += move_vector * dual_step_size\n              \n              # Simple compensation:\
    \ move nearest overlap neighbor slightly inwards\n              distances_to_idx = np.linalg.norm(current_centers - current_centers[idx], axis=1)\n              distances_to_idx[idx] = np.inf\n              \n              closest_overlap_neighbor_idx = -1\n              min_dist_to_overlap_neighbor = np.inf\n              # Need current radii to assess 'overlap'\n              temp_radii, _, _ = compute_max_radii(current_centers)\n              for other_idx in range(n):\n                  if other_idx == idx: continue\n                  if distances_to_idx[other_idx] - (temp_radii[idx] + temp_radii[other_idx]) < 1e-7: # Check if in near overlap\n                      if distances_to_idx[other_idx] < min_dist_to_overlap_neighbor:\n                          closest_overlap_neighbor_idx = other_idx\n                          min_dist_to_overlap_neighbor = distances_to_idx[other_idx]\n              \n              if closest_overlap_neighbor_idx != -1:\n                  compensation_vec\
    \ = current_centers[idx] - current_centers[closest_overlap_neighbor_idx]\n                  unit_compensation_vec = compensation_vec / (np.linalg.norm(compensation_vec) + 1e-10)\n                  candidate_centers[closest_overlap_neighbor_idx] -= unit_compensation_vec * (dual_step_size / 2.0)\n\n              move_applied = True\n\n          elif max_dual_idx_type[0] == 'overlap':\n              idx1, idx2 = max_dual_idx_type[1], max_dual_idx_type[2]\n              \n              # Move circles apart along their connecting vector\n              vec = current_centers[idx1] - current_centers[idx2]\n              norm_vec = np.linalg.norm(vec)\n              if norm_vec > 1e-10:\n                  unit_vec = vec / norm_vec\n                  candidate_centers[idx1] += unit_vec * (dual_step_size / 2)\n                  candidate_centers[idx2] -= unit_vec * (dual_step_size / 2)\n                  move_applied = True\n              else: # If centers are coincident, apply a small random\
    \ perturbation\n                  candidate_centers[idx1] += rng.normal(0, dual_step_size / 2, 2)\n                  candidate_centers[idx2] += rng.normal(0, dual_step_size / 2, 2)\n                  move_applied = True # Count as a move\n\n          candidate_centers = np.clip(candidate_centers, clip_margin, 1 - clip_margin)\n          new_score = objective_function_for_minimize(candidate_centers.flatten())\n          \n          # LP-Gated Acceptance with min_slack check\n          if new_score < current_score:\n              temp_radii, _, _ = compute_max_radii(candidate_centers)\n              current_min_slack = calculate_min_slack_evaluator_style(candidate_centers, temp_radii * (1.0 - 1e-8)) # Evaluate after shrink\n              if current_min_slack >= min_slack_for_persistence:\n                  current_centers = candidate_centers\n                  current_score = new_score\n                  # print(f\"    Dual Refine iter {iter_refine}: score improved to {-current_score:.7f},\
    \ min_slack={current_min_slack:.2e}\")\n              else:\n                  # print(f\"    Dual Refine iter {iter_refine}: score improved but min_slack ({current_min_slack:.2e}) insufficient. Rejecting.\")\n                  pass # Don't update current_centers/score\n          else:\n              # print(f\"    Dual Refine iter {iter_refine}: no improvement.\")\n              pass\n\n\n      return current_centers, current_score\n\n\n  # --- Artifact Persistence Functions ---\n  ARTIFACT_PATH = 'storage/Quest/sumr32_best.npz'\n  MIN_DELTA_SCORE_FOR_PERSISTENCE = 1e-8\n  MIN_SLACK_FOR_PERSISTENCE = 1e-10 \n\n  def load_best_artifact():\n      if os.path.exists(ARTIFACT_PATH):\n          data = np.load(ARTIFACT_PATH)\n          return data['centers'], data['radii'], np.sum(data['radii'])\n      return None, None, -np.inf\n\n  def save_best_artifact(centers: np.ndarray, radii: np.ndarray, score: float):\n      np.savez(ARTIFACT_PATH, centers=centers, radii=radii, score=score)\n    \
    \  print(f\"Artifact saved to {ARTIFACT_PATH} with score {score:.7f}\")\n\n  # --- Parallel Worker Function for Stage 1 SLSQP ---\n  def _run_slsqp_worker(args):\n      initial_x0_flat, bounds_for_optimizer, maxiter_slsqp_stage1, seed, warp_matrix, inv_warp_matrix, is_warped_seed = args\n      np.random.seed(seed) # Ensure deterministic behavior for each worker\n\n      if is_warped_seed:\n          initial_centers_original = initial_x0_flat.reshape(32, 2)\n          initial_centers_centered = initial_centers_original - 0.5\n          initial_x0_optim_flat = (warp_matrix @ initial_centers_centered.T).T.flatten() + 0.5\n      else:\n          initial_x0_optim_flat = initial_x0_flat \n\n\n      def current_optim_objective(flat_optim_centers): \n          if is_warped_seed:\n              optim_centers_warped = flat_optim_centers.reshape(32, 2) - 0.5\n              original_centers = (inv_warp_matrix @ optim_centers_warped.T).T + 0.5\n          else:\n              original_centers = flat_optim_centers.reshape(32,\
    \ 2)\n          \n          original_centers_clipped = np.clip(original_centers, bounds_for_optimizer[0][0], bounds_for_optimizer[0][1])\n          return objective_function_for_minimize(original_centers_clipped.flatten())\n\n      def current_optim_gradient(flat_optim_centers): \n          return gradient_finite_difference(flat_optim_centers)\n\n      optim_bounds_per_coord = (bounds_for_optimizer[0][0], bounds_for_optimizer[0][1])\n      optim_bounds_for_optimizer = [optim_bounds_per_coord] * (32 * 2)\n\n\n      res = minimize(\n          current_optim_objective, \n          initial_x0_optim_flat, \n          method='SLSQP',\n          jac=current_optim_gradient, \n          bounds=optim_bounds_for_optimizer,\n          options={'maxiter': maxiter_slsqp_stage1, 'disp': False}\n      )\n      \n      if res.success:\n          optimized_optim_flat = res.x\n          if is_warped_seed:\n              optimized_optim_centers = optimized_optim_flat.reshape(32, 2) - 0.5\n              optimized_centers_original\
    \ = (inv_warp_matrix @ optimized_optim_centers.T).T + 0.5\n          else:\n              optimized_centers_original = optimized_optim_flat.reshape(32, 2)\n              \n          optimized_centers_final = np.clip(optimized_centers_original, bounds_for_optimizer[0][0], bounds_for_optimizer[0][1])\n\n          radii, lp_success, _ = compute_max_radii(optimized_centers_final)\n          if not lp_success:\n              radii = compute_max_radii_heuristic(optimized_centers_final)\n          explicit_safe_radii = radii * (1.0 - 1e-8)\n          return np.sum(explicit_safe_radii), optimized_centers_final\n      else:\n          return -np.inf, initial_centers_original if is_warped_seed else initial_x0_flat.reshape(32, 2)\n\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      n = 32\n      \n      # Configuration Parameters (for transparent versioning)\n      CONFIGURATION_PARAMS = {\n          'clip_margin': 1e-7,\n          'perturbation_strength_init': 0.05,\n          'num_parallel_starts':\
    \ 128, # Reverting to 128 starts\n          'maxiter_slsqp_stage1': 175, # Reverting to 175 iterations per parallel start\n          'maxiter_slsqp_final': 750, # Reverting to 750 deep refinement iterations\n          'num_dual_refine_iterations': 500, # New parameter for dual refinement\n          'dual_step_size': 1e-5, # New parameter for dual refinement\n          'micro_global_perturb_strength': 1e-6,\n          'contact_threshold': 1e-7,\n          'triad_formation_threshold': 5e-7,\n          'refinement_seed': 1999,\n          'warp_scale_x': 1.1,\n          'warp_scale_y': 0.9,\n          'warp_shear_xy': 0.1,\n          'warp_rotation_angle_deg': 5.0,\n          'lp_safety_margin_internal': 4e-9,\n          'explicit_safety_shrink_factor_obj': 1.0 - 1e-8,\n          'min_delta_score_for_persistence': 1e-8,\n          'min_slack_for_persistence': 1e-10,\n          'radii_shrink_factor_final_return': 1.0 - 1e-12,\n      }\n\n      # Unpack parameters into local variables\n  \
    \    clip_margin = CONFIGURATION_PARAMS['clip_margin']\n      perturbation_strength_init = CONFIGURATION_PARAMS['perturbation_strength_init']\n      num_parallel_starts = CONFIGURATION_PARAMS['num_parallel_starts']\n      maxiter_slsqp_stage1 = CONFIGURATION_PARAMS['maxiter_slsqp_stage1']\n      maxiter_slsqp_final = CONFIGURATION_PARAMS['maxiter_slsqp_final']\n      num_dual_refine_iterations = CONFIGURATION_PARAMS['num_dual_refine_iterations']\n      dual_step_size = CONFIGURATION_PARAMS['dual_step_size']\n      micro_global_perturb_strength = CONFIGURATION_PARAMS['micro_global_perturb_strength']\n      contact_threshold = CONFIGURATION_PARAMS['contact_threshold']\n      triad_formation_threshold = CONFIGURATION_PARAMS['triad_formation_threshold']\n      refinement_seed = CONFIGURATION_PARAMS['refinement_seed']\n      warp_scale_x = CONFIGURATION_PARAMS['warp_scale_x']\n      warp_scale_y = CONFIGURATION_PARAMS['warp_scale_y']\n      warp_shear_xy = CONFIGURATION_PARAMS['warp_shear_xy']\n\
    \      warp_rotation_angle_deg = CONFIGURATION_PARAMS['warp_rotation_angle_deg']\n      lp_safety_margin_internal = CONFIGURATION_PARAMS['lp_safety_margin_internal']\n      radii_shrink_factor_final_return_local = CONFIGURATION_PARAMS['radii_shrink_factor_final_return']\n\n\n      # Create deterministic warp and inverse warp matrices\n      rotation_rad = np.deg2rad(warp_rotation_angle_deg)\n      R = np.array([\n          [np.cos(rotation_rad), -np.sin(rotation_rad)],\n          [np.sin(rotation_rad), np.cos(rotation_rad)]\n      ])\n      S = np.array([\n          [warp_scale_x, warp_shear_xy],\n          [0.0, warp_scale_y]\n      ])\n      warp_matrix = R @ S\n      inv_warp_matrix = np.linalg.inv(warp_matrix)\n\n      global_best_score = -np.inf\n      global_best_centers = None\n      global_best_radii = None\n\n      # --- Loader-First Policy ---\n      persisted_centers, persisted_radii, persisted_score = load_best_artifact()\n      if persisted_centers is not None and persisted_radii\
    \ is not None and persisted_score > -np.inf:\n          print(f\"Loaded persisted artifact with score: {persisted_score:.7f}. Returning this artifact directly.\")\n          return persisted_centers, persisted_radii * radii_shrink_factor_final_return_local\n\n      print(\"No artifact found or forced search. Starting full optimization.\")\n      \n      persisted_score = -np.inf \n\n      bounds_per_coord = (clip_margin, 1 - clip_margin)\n      bounds_for_optimizer = [bounds_per_coord] * (n * 2) \n\n      # --- Stage 1: Massively Parallel Multi-Start SLSQP ---\n      print(f\"Starting Stage 1: Massively Parallel Multi-Start SLSQP with {num_parallel_starts} starts (including warped seeds)\")\n      \n      initial_x0_list = []\n      is_warped_seed_list = []\n      for i in range(num_parallel_starts):\n          seed_val = i + 1000 \n          np.random.seed(seed_val)\n          \n          seed_type = i % 4 \n          if seed_type == 0: \n              initial_centers = get_perturbed_grid_centers(n,\
    \ clip_margin, perturbation_strength_init, seed_val)\n              is_warped_seed_list.append(False)\n          elif seed_type == 1: \n              initial_centers = get_row_pattern_centers(n, clip_margin, seed_val)\n              is_warped_seed_list.append(False)\n          elif seed_type == 2: \n              initial_centers = get_farthest_point_centers(n, clip_margin, seed_val)\n              is_warped_seed_list.append(False)\n          else: \n              initial_centers = get_warped_grid_centers(n, int(np.sqrt(n)), warp_scale_x, warp_scale_y, warp_shear_xy, warp_rotation_angle_deg, clip_margin, seed_val)\n              is_warped_seed_list.append(True) \n          \n          initial_x0_list.append(initial_centers.flatten())\n\n      worker_args = [\n          (x0_flat, bounds_for_optimizer, maxiter_slsqp_stage1, i + 3000, warp_matrix, inv_warp_matrix, is_warped_seed_list[i]) \n          for i, x0_flat in enumerate(initial_x0_list)\n      ]\n\n      with mp.Pool(processes=num_parallel_starts)\
    \ as pool:\n          results_list = pool.map(_run_slsqp_worker, worker_args)\n      \n      best_stage1_score = -np.inf\n      best_stage1_centers = None\n      for score, centers in results_list:\n          if score > best_stage1_score:\n              best_stage1_score = score\n              best_stage1_centers = centers\n      \n      print(f\"Stage 1 Parallel SLSQP completed. Best score found = {best_stage1_score:.4f}\")\n      if best_stage1_centers is None: \n          best_stage1_centers = np.random.rand(n, 2)\n          best_stage1_score = objective_function_for_minimize(best_stage1_centers.flatten()) \n          print(\"Warning: All parallel SLSQP runs failed. Using a random fallback.\")\n\n      # --- Stage 2: Dedicated Deep SLSQP Refinement ---\n      print(\"\\nStarting Stage 2: Dedicated Deep SLSQP Refinement\")\n      \n      initial_x0_final_slsqp = best_stage1_centers.flatten()\n\n      res = minimize(\n          objective_function_for_minimize,\n          initial_x0_final_slsqp,\n\
    \          method='SLSQP',\n          jac=gradient_finite_difference, \n          bounds=bounds_for_optimizer,\n          options={'maxiter': maxiter_slsqp_final, 'disp': False} \n      )\n\n      if res.success:\n          optimized_centers_flat = res.x\n          optimized_centers = optimized_centers_flat.reshape(n, 2)\n          # --- Post-SLSQP Dual-Informed Refinement ---\n          print(f\"  Stage 2: Starting Dual-Informed Refinement.\")\n          refined_centers_after_dual, refined_score_after_dual = dual_informed_refinement(\n              optimized_centers,\n              objective_function_for_minimize(optimized_centers_flat), # Pass negative score\n              num_dual_refine_iterations,\n              dual_step_size,\n              clip_margin,\n              refinement_seed,\n              MIN_SLACK_FOR_PERSISTENCE # Pass persistence slack for internal check\n          )\n          final_optimized_centers = refined_centers_after_dual\n          final_lp_score_neg = refined_score_after_dual\
    \ \n\n          final_radii_exact, final_lp_success, _ = compute_max_radii(final_optimized_centers)\n          \n          if not final_lp_success: \n              print(f\"Stage 2 Final LP failed for optimized centers, falling back to heuristic for radii.\")\n              final_radii_exact = compute_max_radii_heuristic(final_optimized_centers)\n\n          explicit_safe_radii = final_radii_exact * (1.0 - 1e-8) \n          current_score = np.sum(explicit_safe_radii)\n          \n          print(f\"Full Optimization (Parallel SLSQP + Deep SLSQP + Dual-Informed) successful, score = {current_score:.4f}\")\n          if current_score > global_best_score:\n              global_best_score = current_score\n              global_best_centers = final_optimized_centers\n              global_best_radii = explicit_safe_radii \n      else:\n          print(f\"Stage 2 Deep SLSQP Optimization failed: {res.message}. Using best from Stage 1 for comparison (before dual-informed refinement).\")\n     \
    \     # If deep SLSQP fails, use the best from Stage 1 and still try dual-informed refinement\n          refined_centers_after_dual, refined_score_after_dual = dual_informed_refinement(\n              best_stage1_centers,\n              objective_function_for_minimize(best_stage1_centers.flatten()), # Pass negative score\n              num_dual_refine_iterations,\n              dual_step_size,\n              clip_margin,\n              refinement_seed,\n              MIN_SLACK_FOR_PERSISTENCE\n          )\n          final_optimized_centers_fallback = refined_centers_after_dual\n          final_radii_exact_fallback, final_lp_success_fallback, _ = compute_max_radii(final_optimized_centers_fallback)\n          if not final_lp_success_fallback:\n              final_radii_exact_fallback = compute_max_radii_heuristic(final_optimized_centers_fallback)\n          explicit_safe_radii_fallback = final_radii_exact_fallback * (1.0 - 1e-8)\n\n          current_score = np.sum(explicit_safe_radii_fallback)\n\
    \          if current_score > global_best_score:\n              global_best_score = current_score\n              global_best_centers = final_optimized_centers_fallback\n              global_best_radii = explicit_safe_radii_fallback\n              \n      # --- Persistence Check ---\n      if global_best_centers is not None and global_best_radii is not None:\n          current_min_slack = calculate_min_slack_evaluator_style(global_best_centers, global_best_radii)\n          \n          if (global_best_score > persisted_score + MIN_DELTA_SCORE_FOR_PERSISTENCE) and (current_min_slack >= MIN_SLACK_FOR_PERSISTENCE):\n              save_best_artifact(global_best_centers, global_best_radii, global_best_score)\n          else:\n              print(f\"Current best score ({global_best_score:.7f}) not significantly better than persisted ({persisted_score:.7f}) or min slack ({current_min_slack:.2e}) insufficient ({MIN_SLACK_FOR_PERSISTENCE:.2e} required). Not persisting.\")\n\n      if global_best_radii\
    \ is not None:\n          global_best_radii_return = global_best_radii * (1.0 - 1e-12)\n          return global_best_centers, global_best_radii_return\n      \n      return global_best_centers, global_best_radii\n```"
