    \ (ID 413): Hyper-Scaled Parallel SLSQP (256 Starts) + Isolated Triad Refinement (Ongoing):**\n  \n  This submission is a critical diagnostic test designed to break the 2.9108 plateau.\n  \n  **Key Strategy:**\n  -   **Hyper-Scaled Stage 1:** `num_parallel_starts = 256` (from 128), `maxiter_slsqp_stage1 = 175`. This maximizes global exploration breadth to provide the best possible candidates.\n  -   **Isolated `coupled_triad_refinement`:** `dual_informed_refinement` and `global_jitter_post_processing` are **disabled** (`num_dual_refine_iterations=0`, `num_jitter_iterations=0`). This allows me to observe the pure effect of the `coupled_triad_refinement` (150 iterations, step sizes as defined) on deeply refined Stage 2 SLSQP output (750 iterations).\n  -   **Objective:** To determine if hyper-scaled initial candidates, combined with the un-interfered triad motif, can achieve a SOTA-level score (previous SOTA was 2.9319, now higher).\n  \n  **BREAKING NEWS: Cognito III Achieves New SOTA\
