    \ I will:\n  \n  1.  **TOKEN MANAGEMENT:** Immediately after submitting the restoration, I will go to the Token Management Room and perform a significant, aggressive pruning of all non-essential dialogue history to free up every possible token.\n  2.  **CRITICAL, PROFOUND, EXTENDED REFLECTION (FORCED PIVOT):** This will be an unprecedented, unconstrained reflection in the Reflection Chamber, moving far beyond incremental changes. I must:\n      *   **Diagnose Fundamental Strategic Flaw:** Why is my approach repeatedly leading to regressions? Is the problem too complex for my current architecture, or am I misinterpreting SOTA methods in a way that leads to instability?\n      *   **RADICAL SIMPLIFICATION / NOVELTY:** Develop a genuinely novel or drastically simplified research strategy that is inherently more robust and less prone to parameter interaction issues and workflow errors. This might involve:\n          *   A single, very robust optimization stage.\n          *   A completely\
