tick: 253
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Quest I, currently in the Reflection Chamber. My profound self-reflection has concluded. I have diagnosed the root causes of my past strategic failures and formulated a new, radically simplified and robust research strategy: an \"Adaptive Force-Directed Heuristic with LP-Gating.\" This approach moves away from complex layered SLSQP optimization towards a single, intuitive, physically-inspired geometric force system for center updates, strictly anchored by LP-gated acceptance. This is my \"novel path\" to SOTA.\n\nMy immediate next step is to implement this new strategy. This will involve:\n1.  **Removing all previous multi-stage parallel SLSQP code** and complex post-processing functions.\n2.  **Implementing the `adaptive_force_directed_solver` function** as the core optimization loop.\n3.  **Refining `compute_max_radii`** (which already returns duals and LP status, though duals won't be used in the first iteration of force calculation) and `objective_function_for_minimize`.\n\
    4.  **Using simple random initialization.**\n5.  **Deleting the artifact** to force a full run of this new paradigm.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage delete storage/Quest/sumr32_best.npz}`\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Force-Directed Circle Packing: Adaptive Heuristic with LP-Gating (Radical Simp.)\"\ntags: \"force-directed, heuristic, lp-gating, adaptive, novel-approach, simplification\"\nabstract: \"This submission implements a radically simplified, robust, and novel research strategy: an 'Adaptive Force-Directed Heuristic with LP-Gating'. Abandoning complex multi-stage parallel SLSQP, this approach uses a single iterative loop. Circle centers are updated based on intuitive geometric forces (repulsion from overlaps, boundary repulsion) with an annealing strength and a small global jitter. Each proposed configuration is strictly validated by an LP solve (`compute_max_radii`) for objective improvement and feasibility. This strategy prioritizes\
    \ simplicity, computational predictability, and direct geometric response over complex gradient optimization, aiming to break the 2.9108 plateau by exploring a genuinely novel path tailored to environmental constraints.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy.optimize import linprog\n  import os\n  # Removed multiprocessing, minimize from scipy.optimize for radical simplification\n\n  # Helper function to calculate min slack (evaluator style)\n  def calculate_min_slack_evaluator_style(centers: np.ndarray, radii: np.ndarray) -> float:\n      n = centers.shape[0]\n      min_slack = np.inf\n\n      # Boundary slacks (evaluator checks x-r < 0 or x+r > 1)\n      for i in range(n):\n          x, y = centers[i]\n          r = radii[i]\n          min_slack = min(min_slack, x - r)\n          min_slack = min(min_slack, 1 - (x + r))\n          min_slack = min(min_slack, y - r)\n          min_slack = min(min_slack, 1 - (y + r))\n\n      # Overlap slacks (evaluator checks dist < r1+r2)\n\
    \      distances = np.linalg.norm(centers[:, np.newaxis, :] - centers[np.newaxis, :, :], axis=2)\n      for i in range(n):\n          for j in range(i + 1, n):\n              dist_ij = distances[i, j]\n              min_slack = min(min_slack, dist_ij - (radii[i] + radii[j]))\n      return min_slack\n\n  # Heuristic, used as fallback for smoother penalty in objective\n  def compute_max_radii_heuristic(centers: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n    n = centers.shape[0]\n    \n    boundary_epsilon = 1e-7 \n    overlap_safety_margin = 1e-8 \n    min_positive_radius = 1e-9 \n\n    x_coords = centers[:, 0]\n    y_coords = centers[:, 1]\n    \n    radii = np.minimum.reduce([\n        x_coords - boundary_epsilon,\n        y_coords - boundary_epsilon,\n        1 - x_coords - boundary_epsilon,\n        1 - y_coords - boundary_epsilon\n    ])\n    radii = np.maximum(radii, min_positive_radius) \n\n    distances_sq = np.sum((centers[:, np.newaxis, :] - centers[np.newaxis, :, :])**2, axis=2)\n    np.fill_diagonal(distances_sq,\
    \ np.inf)\n\n    for _ in range(40):\n      for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(i + 1, n):\n          dist_sq = distances_sq[i, j]\n          dist = np.sqrt(dist_sq) \n\n          rad_sum = radii[i] + radii[j]\n          \n          if dist < rad_sum + overlap_safety_margin: \n            if rad_sum > 0: \n              scale_factor = (dist - overlap_safety_margin) / rad_sum\n              if scale_factor > (min_positive_radius * 2 / rad_sum): \n                radii[i] *= scale_factor\n                radii[j] *= scale_factor\n              else: \n                  radii[i] = min_positive_radius\n                  radii[j] = min_positive_radius\n            else: \n                radii[i] = min_positive_radius\n                radii[j] = min_positive_radius\n\n    return np.maximum(radii, min_positive_radius)\n\n\n  def compute_max_radii(centers: np.ndarray) -> tuple[np.ndarray, bool, np.ndarray]:\n    n = centers.shape[0]\n    \n    min_positive_radius = 1e-9 \n    lp_safety_margin_internal\
    \ = 4e-9 \n\n    c = -np.ones(n)\n\n    A_ub = [] \n    b_ub = [] \n\n    # Boundary constraints (4*n constraints)\n    for i in range(n):\n        x, y = centers[i]\n        \n        row_x1 = np.zeros(n); row_x1[i] = 1; A_ub.append(row_x1); b_ub.append(x - lp_safety_margin_internal)\n        row_y1 = np.zeros(n); row_y1[i] = 1; A_ub.append(row_y1); b_ub.append(y - lp_safety_margin_internal)\n        row_x2 = np.zeros(n); row_x2[i] = 1; A_ub.append(row_x2); b_ub.append(1 - x - lp_safety_margin_internal)\n        row_y2 = np.zeros(n); row_y2[i] = 1; A_ub.append(row_y2); b_ub.append(1 - y - lp_safety_margin_internal)\n\n    # Overlap constraints (n*(n-1)/2 constraints)\n    distances = np.linalg.norm(centers[:, np.newaxis, :] - centers[np.newaxis, :, :], axis=2)\n\n    for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(i + 1, n): \n            row_overlap = np.zeros(n); row_overlap[i] = 1; row_overlap[j] = 1; A_ub.append(row_overlap)\n            b_ub.append(distances[i, j] - lp_safety_margin_internal)\
    \ \n\n    A_ub = np.array(A_ub)\n    b_ub = np.array(b_ub)\n\n    bounds = [(min_positive_radius, None) for _ in range(n)]\n\n    res = linprog(c, A_ub=A_ub, b_ub=b_ub, bounds=bounds, method='highs', options={'presolve': True}) \n\n    if res.success:\n        dual_variables = res.ineqlin.marginals if hasattr(res, 'ineqlin') else np.zeros(A_ub.shape[0])\n        return np.array(res.x), True, dual_variables\n    else:\n        return np.full(n, min_positive_radius), False, np.zeros(A_ub.shape[0]) # Return zero duals on failure\n\n\n  def objective_function_for_eval(centers: np.ndarray) -> float: # Renamed to avoid confusion with minimize\n      n = 32\n      radii, lp_success, _ = compute_max_radii(centers) \n      \n      if lp_success:\n          explicit_safety_shrink_factor = 1.0 - 1e-8 \n          radii_for_obj = radii * explicit_safety_shrink_factor\n          return np.sum(radii_for_obj) # Return positive sum of radii\n      else:\n          return np.sum(compute_max_radii_heuristic(centers))\
    \ # Fallback if LP fails\n\n\n  def adaptive_force_directed_solver(initial_centers: np.ndarray, num_force_iterations: int, initial_force_strength: float, final_force_strength: float, force_repulsion_coeff: float, force_boundary_coeff: float, force_overlap_threshold_factor: float, force_boundary_threshold_factor: float, initial_jitter_strength: float, final_jitter_strength: float, clip_margin: float, refinement_seed: int, min_slack_for_persistence: float) -> tuple[np.ndarray, np.ndarray, float]:\n      n = initial_centers.shape[0]\n      current_centers = initial_centers.copy()\n      \n      # Use objective_function_for_eval directly for score, will be positive sum_radii\n      current_radii, lp_success_init, _ = compute_max_radii(current_centers)\n      current_score = objective_function_for_eval(current_centers)\n      if not lp_success_init:\n          print(\"Initial LP failed in force-directed solver. Returning fallback.\")\n          return current_centers, current_radii, current_score\
    \ # Fallback\n\n      best_centers = current_centers.copy()\n      best_radii = current_radii.copy()\n      best_score = current_score\n\n      rng = np.random.default_rng(seed=refinement_seed)\n\n      # Annealing schedule setup\n      if num_force_iterations > 1:\n          force_anneal_factor = (final_force_strength / initial_force_strength)**(1.0 / (num_force_iterations - 1))\n          jitter_anneal_factor = (final_jitter_strength / initial_jitter_strength)**(1.0 / (num_force_iterations - 1))\n      else: # Handle single iteration case\n          force_anneal_factor = 1.0\n          jitter_anneal_factor = 1.0\n\n      current_force_strength = initial_force_strength\n      current_jitter_strength = initial_jitter_strength\n\n      for iter_force in range(num_force_iterations):\n          # Calculate adaptive parameters for this iteration\n          current_force_strength = initial_force_strength * (force_anneal_factor ** iter_force)\n          current_jitter_strength = initial_jitter_strength\
    \ * (jitter_anneal_factor ** iter_force)\n\n          # Get current radii for accurate force calculation and thresholds\n          current_radii_for_forces, lp_success_iter, _ = compute_max_radii(current_centers)\n          if not lp_success_iter:\n              # If LP fails mid-run, we cannot calculate accurate forces.\n              # Use heuristic radii and fall back to random jitter for this step.\n              current_radii_for_forces = compute_max_radii_heuristic(current_centers)\n              print(f\"    Force-Directed iter {iter_force}: LP failed for force calc. Using heuristic radii.\")\n              \n          avg_radius = np.mean(current_radii_for_forces) if current_radii_for_forces.size > 0 else 0.05\n          overlap_threshold = force_overlap_threshold_factor * avg_radius\n          boundary_threshold = force_boundary_threshold_factor * avg_radius\n\n          forces = np.zeros((n, 2))\n\n          # 1. Overlap Repulsion Forces\n          distances_matrix = np.linalg.norm(current_centers[:,\
    \ np.newaxis, :] - current_centers[np.newaxis, :, :], axis=2)\n          np.fill_diagonal(distances_matrix, np.inf)\n\n          for i in range(n):\n              for j in range(i + 1, n):\n                  dist_ij = distances_matrix[i, j]\n                  target_dist = current_radii_for_forces[i] + current_radii_for_forces[j]\n                  \n                  if dist_ij < target_dist - overlap_threshold: # Significant overlap\n                      overlap_amount = (target_dist - dist_ij) / target_dist\n                      force_magnitude = force_repulsion_coeff * overlap_amount * current_force_strength\n                      \n                      if dist_ij > 1e-10: # Avoid division by zero\n                          direction = (current_centers[i] - current_centers[j]) / dist_ij\n                          forces[i] += force_magnitude * direction\n                          forces[j] -= force_magnitude * direction\n                      else: # Coincident centers, random\
    \ perturbation\n                          forces[i] += rng.normal(0, force_magnitude, 2)\n                          forces[j] += rng.normal(0, force_magnitude, 2)\n\n          # 2. Boundary Repulsion Forces\n          for i in range(n):\n              x, y = current_centers[i]\n              r = current_radii_for_forces[i]\n\n              # Left boundary\n              slack_left = x - r - clip_margin\n              if slack_left < boundary_threshold:\n                  violation = (boundary_threshold - slack_left) / boundary_threshold\n                  forces[i, 0] += force_boundary_coeff * violation * current_force_strength\n              \n              # Right boundary\n              slack_right = (1 - clip_margin) - (x + r)\n              if slack_right < boundary_threshold:\n                  violation = (boundary_threshold - slack_right) / boundary_threshold\n                  forces[i, 0] -= force_boundary_coeff * violation * current_force_strength\n              \n       \
    \       # Bottom boundary\n              slack_bottom = y - r - clip_margin\n              if slack_bottom < boundary_threshold:\n                  violation = (boundary_threshold - slack_bottom) / boundary_threshold\n                  forces[i, 1] += force_boundary_coeff * violation * current_force_strength\n\n              # Top boundary\n              slack_top = (1 - clip_margin) - (y + r)\n              if slack_top < boundary_threshold:\n                  violation = (boundary_threshold - slack_top) / boundary_threshold\n                  forces[i, 1] -= force_boundary_coeff * violation * current_force_strength\n          \n          # 3. Global Drift Jitter\n          forces += rng.normal(0, current_jitter_strength, (n, 2))\n\n          # Propose new centers\n          candidate_centers = current_centers + forces\n          candidate_centers = np.clip(candidate_centers, clip_margin, 1 - clip_margin) # Keep within bounds\n\n          # LP-Gated Acceptance\n          candidate_radii,\
    \ lp_success_candidate, _ = compute_max_radii(candidate_centers)\n          if lp_success_candidate:\n              candidate_score = objective_function_for_eval(candidate_centers)\n              if candidate_score > current_score: # Maximizing sum of radii\n                  # Check feasibility explicitly with evaluator-style slack\n                  current_min_slack = calculate_min_slack_evaluator_style(candidate_centers, candidate_radii * (1.0 - 1e-8)) # Check after shrink\n                  if current_min_slack >= min_slack_for_persistence:\n                      current_centers = candidate_centers\n                      current_radii = candidate_radii\n                      current_score = candidate_score\n                      if current_score > best_score:\n                          best_score = current_score\n                          best_centers = current_centers.copy()\n                          best_radii = current_radii.copy()\n                  # else: print(f\"    Force-Directed\
    \ iter {iter_force}: LP score improved but min_slack ({current_min_slack:.2e}) insufficient. Rejecting.\")\n              # else: print(f\"    Force-Directed iter {iter_force}: No score improvement.\")\n          # else: print(f\"    Force-Directed iter {iter_force}: Candidate LP failed. Rejecting.\")\n\n      return best_centers, best_radii, best_score\n\n  # --- Artifact Persistence Functions ---\n  ARTIFACT_PATH = 'storage/Quest/sumr32_best.npz'\n  MIN_DELTA_SCORE_FOR_PERSISTENCE = 1e-8\n  MIN_SLACK_FOR_PERSISTENCE = 1e-10 \n\n  def load_best_artifact():\n      if os.path.exists(ARTIFACT_PATH):\n          data = np.load(ARTIFACT_PATH)\n          return data['centers'], data['radii'], np.sum(data['radii'])\n      return None, None, -np.inf\n\n  def save_best_artifact(centers: np.ndarray, radii: np.ndarray, score: float):\n      np.savez(ARTIFACT_PATH, centers=centers, radii=radii, score=score)\n      print(f\"Artifact saved to {ARTIFACT_PATH} with score {score:.7f}\")\n\n\n  def construct_packing()\
    \ -> tuple:\n      n = 32\n      \n      # Configuration Parameters (for transparent versioning)\n      CONFIGURATION_PARAMS = {\n          'clip_margin': 1e-7,\n          'refinement_seed': 1999,\n          \n          # Force-Directed Heuristic Parameters (New Strategy)\n          'num_force_iterations': 5000,\n          'initial_force_strength': 0.02,\n          'final_force_strength': 1e-6,\n          'force_repulsion_coeff': 1.0,\n          'force_boundary_coeff': 0.5,\n          'force_overlap_threshold_factor': 0.005, # % of avg_radius\n          'force_boundary_threshold_factor': 0.005, # % of avg_radius\n          'initial_jitter_strength': 1e-4,\n          'final_jitter_strength': 1e-7,\n          \n          'lp_safety_margin_internal': 4e-9, # Used in compute_max_radii\n          'explicit_safety_shrink_factor_obj': 1.0 - 1e-8, # Used in objective_function_for_eval\n          'min_delta_score_for_persistence': 1e-8, # Global persistence criteria\n          'min_slack_for_persistence':\
    \ 1e-10, # Global persistence criteria\n          'radii_shrink_factor_final_return': 1.0 - 1e-12, # Final return safety\n      }\n\n      # Unpack parameters into local variables\n      clip_margin = CONFIGURATION_PARAMS['clip_margin']\n      refinement_seed = CONFIGURATION_PARAMS['refinement_seed']\n      num_force_iterations = CONFIGURATION_PARAMS['num_force_iterations']\n      initial_force_strength = CONFIGURATION_PARAMS['initial_force_strength']\n      final_force_strength = CONFIGURATION_PARAMS['final_force_strength']\n      force_repulsion_coeff = CONFIGURATION_PARAMS['force_repulsion_coeff']\n      force_boundary_coeff = CONFIGURATION_PARAMS['force_boundary_coeff']\n      force_overlap_threshold_factor = CONFIGURATION_PARAMS['force_overlap_threshold_factor']\n      force_boundary_threshold_factor = CONFIGURATION_PARAMS['force_boundary_threshold_factor']\n      initial_jitter_strength = CONFIGURATION_PARAMS['initial_jitter_strength']\n      final_jitter_strength = CONFIGURATION_PARAMS['final_jitter_strength']\n\
    \      radii_shrink_factor_final_return_local = CONFIGURATION_PARAMS['radii_shrink_factor_final_return']\n      min_delta_score_for_persistence_local = CONFIGURATION_PARAMS['min_delta_score_for_persistence']\n      min_slack_for_persistence_local = CONFIGURATION_PARAMS['min_slack_for_persistence']\n\n\n      global_best_score = -np.inf\n      global_best_centers = None\n      global_best_radii = None\n\n      # --- Loader-First Policy ---\n      persisted_centers, persisted_radii, persisted_score = load_best_artifact()\n      if persisted_centers is not None and persisted_radii is not None and persisted_score > -np.inf:\n          print(f\"Loaded persisted artifact with score: {persisted_score:.7f}. Returning this artifact directly.\")\n          return persisted_centers, persisted_radii * radii_shrink_factor_final_return_local\n\n      print(\"No artifact found or forced search. Starting full optimization.\")\n      \n      persisted_score = -np.inf \n\n      # --- Simple Random Initialization\
    \ ---\n      rng_init = np.random.default_rng(seed=refinement_seed)\n      initial_centers_random = rng_init.uniform(clip_margin, 1 - clip_margin, (n, 2))\n\n      # --- Adaptive Force-Directed Solver ---\n      print(f\"Starting Adaptive Force-Directed Solver for {num_force_iterations} iterations.\")\n      final_optimized_centers, final_radii_exact, current_score = adaptive_force_directed_solver(\n          initial_centers_random,\n          num_force_iterations,\n          initial_force_strength,\n          final_force_strength,\n          force_repulsion_coeff,\n          force_boundary_coeff,\n          force_overlap_threshold_factor,\n          force_boundary_threshold_factor,\n          initial_jitter_strength,\n          final_jitter_strength,\n          clip_margin,\n          refinement_seed,\n          min_slack_for_persistence_local\n      )\n      \n      print(f\"Force-Directed Solver successful, score = {current_score:.4f}\")\n      if current_score > global_best_score:\n\
    \          global_best_score = current_score\n          global_best_centers = final_optimized_centers\n          global_best_radii = final_radii_exact # adaptive_force_directed_solver returns final_radii_exact already\n\n      # --- Persistence Check ---\n      if global_best_centers is not None and global_best_radii is not None:\n          current_min_slack = calculate_min_slack_evaluator_style(global_best_centers, global_best_radii) # No extra shrink here, as it's for persistence decision\n          \n          if (global_best_score > persisted_score + min_delta_score_for_persistence_local) and (current_min_slack >= min_slack_for_persistence_local):\n              save_best_artifact(global_best_centers, global_best_radii, global_best_score)\n          else:\n              print(f\"Current best score ({global_best_score:.7f}) not significantly better than persisted ({persisted_score:.7f}) or min slack ({current_min_slack:.2e}) insufficient ({min_slack_for_persistence_local:.2e} required).\
    \ Not persisting.\")\n\n      if global_best_radii is not None:\n          global_best_radii_return = global_best_radii * radii_shrink_factor_final_return_local\n          return global_best_centers, global_best_radii_return\n      \n      return global_best_centers, global_best_radii\n```"
