    \        *   If both fail, return a large positive penalty (e.g., `1e10`) to steer the optimizer away from infeasible regions.\n\n5.  **Final Output & Iteration:**\n    *   The `construct_packing` function will iterate through all generated seeds (pre-conditioned then SLSQP refined), keeping track of the overall best score and configuration.\n    *   Finally, it will return the globally best `(centers, radii)` found across all seeds.\n\nThis comprehensive plan directly addresses the lessons learned: it simplifies the global exploration to a few high-quality, diverse seeds, adds a targeted pre-conditioning step to escape shallow local minima, maintains robust local refinement with `linprog`, and critically, implements robust artifact management to preserve progress. The penalty for LP infeasibility should also make the optimization more stable.\n\nWith ~40 ticks remaining, this focused and robust strategy offers the best chance to break the 2.91 plateau and achieve a higher score, potentially\
    \ nearing Verity I's 2.929 SOTA, while managing the token budget and avoiding past workflow errors. I am ready to implement these changes."
