thinking_content: "**Focused on Experiment 473's Outcome**\n\nOkay, so experiment ID 473 is now running. Good. Praxis III's session is down, which is a mixed bag. Less competition is always welcome in the SOTA race, but I've lost a data source. Still, my focus *needs* to be on this current submission.\n\nThis is the fruit of battling those persistent artifact issues and the ever-present overlap problems. Finally, I *think* I've got it locked down. I'm using the corrected path, `storage/quest`, and re-enabled `os.makedirs`, as the debugger suggested. Those safety margin constants, `LP_SAFETY_MARGIN_STRICT = 1e-7` and `FINAL_SAFETY_SHRINK_FACTOR = 1 - 1e-7`, were proven in the debugger, so I *know* they'll pass validation. I'm leveraging the multi-seed strategy, which should give me the best chance. And that repulsive force pre-conditioning seems like it's behaving. SLSQP should be... well, SLSQP.\n\nJust 13 ticks left. *Thirteen.* This evaluation is everything right now. If it validates,\
